      "label": "Collect focused BloodHound data and validate an attack path",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:S11",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 35,
      "y": 16292,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 838,
      "label": "Interpret an AD trust as a boundary, not a privilege transition",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:S18",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 35,
      "y": 17255,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 838,
      "label": "Inspect AD-integrated DNS record control",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "topic:ad-mapping",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 440,
      "width": 1800,
      "height": 140,
      "text": "# Map Active Directory attack paths\n\nStart with a known domain identity or a directory query context; useful group, object-right and session edges are not assumed.",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-mapping:home",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 240,
      "text": "## Investigation flow\n\nMap Active Directory attack paths\n\n · \n\nBranches describe evidence and missing conditions. Follow one useful lead, then return to unfinished coverage.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-mapping:check-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 560,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 372,
      "text": "## Resolve domain, DC, DNS and clock first\n\nUse the current domain identity or the supported query context; wrong naming/transport can look like a bad password.\n\n```cmd\nwhoami /all\nwhoami /upn\nnltest /dsgetdc:DOMAIN\nw32tm /query /status\n```\n\n**Establish domain identity, DC, DNS, time and route — on this canvas**"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-mapping:check-0-finding-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Domain/DC preflight works\n\nEnumerate users/groups/SPNs and collect supported directory relationships.\n\n**Enumerate directory objects with native, LDAP and PowerView approaches — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-mapping:check-0-fallback",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2380,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Unresolved / alternate check\n\nKDC timeout, name failure or skew: repair that dependency before judging credentials.\n\n**Establish domain identity, DC, DNS, time and route — on this canvas**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-mapping:check-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 560,
      "y": 1172,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "## Collect a BloodHound directory baseline with SharpHound\n\nUse a collector compatible with the BloodHound version. DCOnly is a directory baseline, not proof of all host/session edges.\n\n```powershell\n.\\SharpHound.exe --CollectionMethods DCOnly --OutputDirectory .\\bh --ZipFileName domain-dconly.zip\n```\n\n**Collect focused BloodHound data and validate an attack path — on this canvas**"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-mapping:check-1-finding-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 1172,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### A useful object-control edge\n\nResolve the controlled trustee, target object and effective ACE.\n\n**Validate effective directory-object control — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-mapping:check-1-finding-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 1397,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### A host/session edge\n\nCheck destination rights and session freshness independently.\n\n**Validate host access and volatile session candidates — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-mapping:check-1-finding-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1610,
      "y": 1622,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### An account with an SPN\n\nCheck the actual account/SPN and ticket-request conditions.\n\n**Identify service accounts and SPNs worth investigating — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-mapping:check-1-fallback",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2380,
      "y": 1172,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Unresolved / alternate check\n\nCollection is blocked or incomplete: query the relevant objects manually.\n\n**Enumerate directory objects with native, LDAP and PowerView approaches — on this canvas**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "notes:ad-mapping",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "notes/ad-mapping.md",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 2032,
      "width": 2100,
      "height": 850
    },
    {
      "id": "notes-label:ad-mapping",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2350,
      "y": 2032,
      "width": 1400,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "## Full procedures and alternatives\n\nThe adjacent embedded note is readable here. Scroll inside it for complete variants. Commands and decisions continue below.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-state:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 3307,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Establish domain identity, DC, DNS, time and route\n\nDomain credentials or a domain-joined foothold",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-state:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 3267,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nwhoami /all\nwhoami /upn\nnltest /dsgetdc:DOMAIN\nw32tm /query /status\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-state:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 3247,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe named realm/DC and actual identity establish where directory/authentication checks must run.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-state:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 3493,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCheck DC/service reachability, resolver/SPN naming and clock compatibility, not merely the password.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-state:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 3197,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nA normal bind/ticket request works in the intended realm: continue domain mapping.\n\n**Verify:** Record represented identity, realm, selected DC, resolver, clock and real source route.\n\n[[notes/ad-mapping.md#domain-state|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-state:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 3538,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe credential belongs only to the target-local account: reject the assumed domain identity.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-state:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 3759,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nDC lookup/time failure leaves domain authentication untested.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-state:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 3197,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 372,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```cmd\nwhoami /all\necho %USERDNSDOMAIN%\necho %USERDOMAIN%\necho %LOGONSERVER%\nnltest /dsgetdc:DOMAIN\nnltest /dclist:DOMAIN\nw32tm /query /status\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-mapping.md#domain-state|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-state:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 3659,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Enumerate directory objects with native, LDAP and PowerView approaches\n\n**When:** A directory bind or domain-joined identity can read relevant objects\n\n**Still required:** Correct search base and authentication transport; object/attribute visibility and compatible local utilities\n\n**Enumerate directory objects with native, LDAP and PowerView approaches — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-state:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 3990,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Preserve DNS, Kerberos names and time across a pivot\n\n**When:** An IP connection works while hostname/Kerberos access fails\n\n**Still required:** Reachable correct resolver/KDC path, matching target SPN/hostname, realm configuration and acceptable time\n\n[[tracks/10 Pivoting.canvas|Preserve DNS, Kerberos names and time across a pivot → 10 Pivoting]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-state:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 4297,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Match route, destination service and effective authorization\n\n**When:** A credential appears valid but the destination's usable access is unknown\n\n**Still required:** Real source-to-service route, correct identity context and protocol-specific execution/logon rights\n\n**Match route, destination service and effective authorization — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-directory:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 4928,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Enumerate directory objects with native, LDAP and PowerView approaches\n\nA directory bind or domain-joined identity can read relevant objects",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-directory:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 4888,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nnet user USER /domain\nnet group \"GROUP\" /domain\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-directory:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 4868,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nAccount/group membership supplies a relationship to investigate; nested membership and effective destination rights remain separate.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-directory:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 5114,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify object SID/type, nesting and the exact right granted to that principal.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-directory:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 5152,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```cmd\nnet user /domain\nnet group /domain\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-directory:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 4818,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe membership resolves to a currently effective object/service right: follow that route.\n\n**Verify:** Retain object identifiers, group relationships and actual visibility; distinguish directory facts from inferred execution access.\n\n[[notes/ad-mapping.md#domain-directory|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-directory:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 5159,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe same-named group belongs to another domain or grants no intended right: reject the assumed relationship.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-directory:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 5380,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nPartial visibility or nesting not yet expanded leaves effective membership unresolved.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-directory:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 4818,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 420,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```cmd\nnet user /domain\nnet user USER /domain\nnet group /domain\nnet group \"Domain Admins\" /domain\nnet group \"GROUP\" /domain\nnet accounts /domain\nnltest /domain_trusts /all_trusts\nnet view /domain\nnet view \\\\DC_HOST\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-mapping.md#domain-directory|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-directory:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 5328,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Validate effective directory-object control\n\n**When:** An ACL/graph edge names GenericAll, GenericWrite, WriteDacl, WriteOwner or an extended/property right\n\n**Still required:** Effective trustee membership, target object/type, inheritance/deny behavior and the exact permitted operation\n\n**Validate effective directory-object control — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-directory:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 5659,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate host access and volatile session candidates\n\n**When:** Group-to-host access edges or a privileged user's possible session\n\n**Still required:** Reachable destination service and its actual authorization; session evidence must be current and collection rights sufficient\n\n**Validate host access and volatile session candidates — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-directory:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 5966,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Request a selected service ticket for offline service-account recovery\n\n**When:** A user-owned SPN and a useful service-account relationship\n\n**Still required:** A valid domain authentication/TGT context, reachable KDC, target SPN and a feasible password/encryption candidate strategy\n\n**Request a selected service ticket for offline service-account recovery — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-directory:next-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 6273,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Collect focused BloodHound data and validate an attack path\n\n**When:** Directory relationships are too broad for manual comparison or a candidate chain needs ranking\n\n**Still required:** Compatible collector/deployment, explicit scope, directory rights and separate permission/connectivity for host/session collection\n\n**Collect focused BloodHound data and validate an attack path — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-directory:next-4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 6604,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Identify service accounts and SPNs worth investigating\n\n**When:** User-owned SPNs or service-account clues\n\n**Still required:** Directory visibility and correct service/account association; roasting requires the additional authentication and encryption conditions\n\n**Identify service accounts and SPNs worth investigating — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-directory:next-5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 6911,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Request AS-REP material for an account without preauthentication\n\n**When:** A known user or directory flag indicates Kerberos preauthentication is disabled\n\n**Still required:** Account with preauthentication disabled, KDC reachability and a supported returned encryption type; no-password and authenticated-discovery contexts differ\n\n**Request AS-REP material for an account without preauthentication — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-directory:next-6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 7266,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Conditional: trace GPO control to privileged policy consumption\n\n**When:** A useful linked GPO has a potentially controllable directory or SYSVOL component\n\n**Still required:** Effective rights on the necessary GPO components, applicable target scope/filtering, writable policy artifact and a privileged refresh trigger\n\n**Conditional: trace GPO control to privileged policy consumption — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-directory:next-7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 7621,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Conditional: use a validated delegation or RBCD relationship\n\n**When:** Delegation configuration or computer-object write suggests a Kerberos impersonation path\n\n**Still required:** Exact delegation type; required service/machine identity and key; allowed target/SPN; account flags and KDC policy permit the flow\n\n**Conditional: use a validated delegation or RBCD relationship — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-directory:next-8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 7952,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Conditional: validate an AD CS enrollment-to-authentication path\n\n**When:** A CA/template configuration exposes a plausible certificate identity transition\n\n**Still required:** Effective enrollment/template/CA rights and the exact vulnerable settings; issuance requirements, identity mapping and authentication route must all permit the path\n\n**Conditional: validate an AD CS enrollment-to-authentication path — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-shares:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 8607,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Read domain shares, SYSVOL and NETLOGON for useful artifacts\n\nA valid domain identity and accessible file services",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-shares:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 8567,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nnet view \\\\DC_HOST\ndir \\\\DOMAIN\\SYSVOL\ndir \\\\DOMAIN\\NETLOGON\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-shares:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 8547,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA real domain-readable script gives concrete identity/path leads for credential and host investigation.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-shares:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 8793,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify readable artifact content, whether any secret is current and what account/service it belongs to.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-shares:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 8855,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```cmd\ndir \\\\DOMAIN\\SYSVOL\ndir \\\\DOMAIN\\NETLOGON\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-shares:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 8497,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe artifact yields a typed usable credential or access clue: follow that specific transition.\n\n**Verify:** Prove read access and actual artifact content; keep recovered real secrets private.\n\n[[notes/ad-mapping.md#domain-shares|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-shares:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 8838,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe script only contains non-sensitive public settings: reject a credential-disclosure inference.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-shares:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 9059,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nShare listing denial without a known-path read test does not settle object access.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-shares:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 8497,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```cmd\nnet view \\\\DC_HOST\ndir \\\\DC_HOST\\SYSVOL\ndir \\\\DC_HOST\\NETLOGON\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-mapping.md#domain-shares|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-shares:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 8863,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Classify the artifact and its identity context\n\n**When:** A secret-like value, key file, stored hash, challenge response or ticket\n\n**Still required:** Artifact provenance and format; possible local/domain/application identity and compatible protocol\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify the artifact and its identity context → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-shares:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 9194,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse\n\n**When:** A password tied to a plausible user and service\n\n**Still required:** Correct local/domain/application identity, reachable compatible service, accepted authentication and account state\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-shares:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 9501,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Enumerate SMB/RPC shares, files and identities\n\n**When:** SMB/RPC endpoints, domain clues or new credentials\n\n**Still required:** Reachable SMB/RPC; anonymous, guest, local or domain context must be explicit; share and filesystem ACLs both matter\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Enumerate SMB/RPC shares, files and identities → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-spns:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 10108,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Identify service accounts and SPNs worth investigating\n\nUser-owned SPNs or service-account clues",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-spns:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 10068,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nGet-DomainUser -SPN | Select-Object samaccountname,serviceprincipalname,memberof\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-spns:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 10048,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA user-owned service name identifies a potential ticket/password-recovery target whose rights may be useful.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-spns:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 10294,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCheck actual account type, KDC authentication, encryption type and feasibility; SPN existence alone is not weakness.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-spns:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 10308,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```cmd\nsetspn -Q */*\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-spns:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 9998,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe selected account is requestable and recovery is justified: choose the roast method.\n\n**Verify:** Record SPN, account/object type and relevant privilege relationships before prioritizing recovery.\n\n[[notes/ad-mapping.md#domain-spns|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-spns:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 10339,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe candidate is a strong random machine-account key with no useful recovery rationale: reject the assumed easy-password path.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-spns:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 10560,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nUnknown ownership or unreadable attributes require a narrower directory query.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-spns:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 9998,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```cmd\nsetspn -Q */*\nsetspn -L ACCOUNT\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-mapping.md#domain-spns|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-spns:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 10340,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Request a selected service ticket for offline service-account recovery\n\n**When:** A user-owned SPN and a useful service-account relationship\n\n**Still required:** A valid domain authentication/TGT context, reachable KDC, target SPN and a feasible password/encryption candidate strategy\n\n**Request a selected service ticket for offline service-account recovery — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-spns:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 10647,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Recover passwords with feasible dictionary, rule and mask attacks\n\n**When:** A supported stored verifier or converted protected artifact\n\n**Still required:** Correct format/mode, complete salt/context, justified candidates and an available offline tool/backend\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Recover passwords with feasible dictionary, rule and mask attacks → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-spns:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 10954,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Validate effective directory-object control\n\n**When:** An ACL/graph edge names GenericAll, GenericWrite, WriteDacl, WriteOwner or an extended/property right\n\n**Still required:** Effective trustee membership, target object/type, inheritance/deny behavior and the exact permitted operation\n\n**Validate effective directory-object control — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-acl:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 11585,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Validate effective directory-object control\n\nAn ACL/graph edge names GenericAll, GenericWrite, WriteDacl, WriteOwner or an extended/property right",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-acl:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 11545,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nGet-DomainObjectAcl -Identity TARGET_OBJECT -ResolveGUIDs\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-acl:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 11525,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA DACL-control ACE for a possibly controlled trustee opens an intermediate-right candidate.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-acl:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 11771,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nResolve the ACE's trustee and group nesting, target object class, GUID and inheritance/deny scope. For password reset, group writes or DACL changes open that exact operation's procedure and check its additional conditions before modifying anything.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-acl:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 11475,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe trustee and exact right apply to the target: select the corresponding object transition.\n\n**Verify:** Verify principal, object SID/type and effective permitted modification; preserve original ACL/state before changes.\n\n[[notes/ad-mapping.md#domain-acl|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-acl:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 11816,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe ACE applies to another object type/trustee or is overridden: reject that edge.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-acl:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 12037,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA graph label or unresolved SID does not establish current effective control.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-acl:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 11475,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```powershell\nGet-DomainObjectAcl -Identity TARGET_OBJECT -ResolveGUIDs |\n  Where-Object { $_.ActiveDirectoryRights -match 'GenericAll|GenericWrite|WriteDacl|WriteOwner|ExtendedRight|WriteProperty|Self' } |\n  Select-Object ObjectDN,SecurityIdentifier,ActiveDirectoryRights,ObjectAceType,AceType,IsInherited,InheritanceType\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-mapping.md#domain-acl|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-acl:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 11889,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Reset a target account password through a validated directory right\n\n**When:** A controlled trustee has the effective password-reset right on a useful account\n\n**Still required:** Exact object/right and account state; the disruptive password change is justified within the assigned lab objective\n\n**Reset a target account password through a validated directory right — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-acl:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 12220,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Add a controlled identity to a group through effective membership rights\n\n**When:** A group member-attribute write or equivalent effective right\n\n**Still required:** Exact target group, controlled principal, useful resulting right and a fresh token/logon context\n\n**Add a controlled identity to a group through effective membership rights — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-acl:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 12527,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Convert ownership or DACL control into a narrower useful right\n\n**When:** Effective WriteOwner or WriteDacl on a useful directory object\n\n**Still required:** Correct object/ACE semantics, permission to perform the required intermediate change and a preserved original ACL/owner\n\n**Convert ownership or DACL control into a narrower useful right — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-acl:next-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 12834,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use validated directory replication rights for bounded credential proof\n\n**When:** A principal has the relevant effective replication rights at the domain naming context\n\n**Still required:** Required replication extended rights, DC RPC connectivity and correct domain identity; access to a member server is insufficient\n\n**Use validated directory replication rights for bounded credential proof — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-hosts:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 13465,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Validate host access and volatile session candidates\n\nGroup-to-host access edges or a privileged user's possible session",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-hosts:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 13425,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nnxc smb TARGET -d DOMAIN -u USER -p 'PASSWORD' --shares\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-hosts:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 13405,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA permitted SMB action identifies a host capability; it does not establish RDP/WinRM/SCM rights. Investigate sessions only with a supported, permitted remote query.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-hosts:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 13675,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify actual group effectiveness, service/logon rights, session freshness and collection visibility.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-hosts:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 13665,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```cmd\nwhoami /groups\nnet localgroup Administrators\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-hosts:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 13355,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe intended host service accepts the account and action: use that particular access form.\n\n**Verify:** Record the destination-specific successful action and freshness/limits of session evidence.\n\n[[notes/ad-mapping.md#domain-hosts|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-hosts:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 13696,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nRDP membership does not grant the proposed service-creation right: reject that method.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-hosts:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 13917,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nDenied session enumeration is a visibility limit, not proof that no useful sessions exist.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-hosts:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 13355,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```powershell\nFind-LocalAdminAccess\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-mapping.md#domain-hosts|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-hosts:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 13673,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Obtain an authorized RDP interactive session\n\n**When:** RDP is reachable and the identity may have remote-interactive logon rights\n\n**Still required:** Allowed account/session policy and compatible client/NLA/TLS; hash-based Restricted Admin has additional supported-policy/admin requirements\n\n**Obtain an authorized RDP interactive session — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-hosts:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 14028,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use WinRM, WinRS or PowerShell remoting\n\n**When:** A WinRM listener and a candidate endpoint-authorized account\n\n**Still required:** Reachable HTTP(S) listener, accepted authentication and endpoint/session configuration permissions; hash/ticket support depends on client/context\n\n**Use WinRM, WinRS or PowerShell remoting — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-hosts:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 14359,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Obtain accessible live logon-session credential material\n\n**When:** A controlled Windows host may hold useful logged-on identities\n\n**Still required:** Required process/host privileges, useful sessions and compatible architecture; PPL/Credential Guard/protection may prevent access or remove material\n\n**Obtain accessible live logon-session credential material — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-graph:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 14990,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Collect focused BloodHound data and validate an attack path\n\nDirectory relationships are too broad for manual comparison or a candidate chain needs ranking",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-graph:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 14950,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nIn BloodHound: locate the controlled principal; inspect the exact edge, source object, destination and collection age.\nResolve its underlying group/ACL/service evidence with the corresponding manual method.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-graph:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 14930,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe directory edge supplies a candidate intermediate right; missing host/session evidence cannot be invented from the graph.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-graph:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 15176,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCollect with a version-compatible SharpHound/BloodHound collector, then validate the selected edge. Resolve group nesting and effective ACEs for object control; test destination rights and session freshness for host/session edges.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-graph:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 15238,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```powershell\nSharpHound.exe --help\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-graph:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 14880,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nEvery relevant edge is current and enabled: rank the connected path against alternatives.\n\n**Verify:** Validate every useful edge against current directory/host evidence and identify the transition each one enables.\n\n[[notes/ad-mapping.md#domain-graph|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-graph:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 15221,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nOne edge is stale or ineffective: reject that chain in its current form.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-graph:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 15418,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA missing edge in partial collection leaves capability unknown, not absent.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-graph:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 14880,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```powershell\n.\\SharpHound.exe --CollectionMethods DCOnly --OutputDirectory .\\bh --ZipFileName domain-dconly.zip\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-mapping.md#domain-graph|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-graph:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 15198,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Validate effective directory-object control\n\n**When:** An ACL/graph edge names GenericAll, GenericWrite, WriteDacl, WriteOwner or an extended/property right\n\n**Still required:** Effective trustee membership, target object/type, inheritance/deny behavior and the exact permitted operation\n\n**Validate effective directory-object control — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-graph:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 15529,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate host access and volatile session candidates\n\n**When:** Group-to-host access edges or a privileged user's possible session\n\n**Still required:** Reachable destination service and its actual authorization; session evidence must be current and collection rights sufficient\n\n**Validate host access and volatile session candidates — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:domain-graph:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 15836,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Maintain state and select the next evidence-producing test\n\n**When:** Several hosts, identities, routes or competing hypotheses need coordination\n\n**Still required:** Explicit scope/objective and a record of observations, unknowns and available capabilities\n\n[[tracks/12 Evidence and Reporting.canvas|Maintain state and select the next evidence-producing test → 12 Evidence and Reporting]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S11:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 16467,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Interpret an AD trust as a boundary, not a privilege transition\n\ndirectory or native trust enumeration identifies another domain/forest relationship.",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S11:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 16427,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nSee the linked discovery procedure.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S11:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 16407,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nrecord source and destination domain, direction, trust type/transitivity, same-forest versus cross-forest context, selective authentication and SID filtering.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S11:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 16677,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\ndestination DNS/KDC/service reachability, accepted identity, target SPN, allowed-to-authenticate/resource rights and the exact capability sought. A trust object or child-domain administration is not automatically forest compromise.\nACTION PROCEDURE PENDING: discovery/validation only.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S11:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 16357,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\ndestination service accepts the identity and action → D29; filtering/selective-auth/resource authorization decisively denies it → ruled out here; direction/filtering/identity or route unresolved → inconclusive.\n\n**Verify:** establish one destination service action under the named identity. Trust-key/SID-history forgery and coercion chains are not registered complete procedures; see RW04.\n\n[[notes/ad-mapping.md#S11|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S11:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 16746,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nFollow the denied/absent-condition outcome in the linked procedure.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S11:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 16943,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nResolve the missing condition; do not infer execution from visibility.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S18:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 70,
      "y": 17430,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Inspect AD-integrated DNS record control\n\nAD-integrated DNS is present and a selected zone or record object may be writable by the current principal.",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S18:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 570,
      "y": 17390,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\n$Root = (Get-ADRootDSE).defaultNamingContext\n  $DnsBase = \"CN=MicrosoftDNS,DC=DomainDnsZones,$Root\"\n  Get-ADObject -SearchBase $DnsBase -LDAPFilter '(objectClass=dnsNode)' -Properties dnsRecord -ResultSetSize 50\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S18:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 17370,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nenumerate the zone container and record objects from a domain Windows context:\n\n  powershell\n  $Root = (Get-ADRootDSE).defaultNamingContext\n  $DnsBase = \"CN=MicrosoftDNS,DC=DomainDnsZones,$Root\"\n  Get-ADObject -SearchBase $DnsBase -LDAPFilter '(objectClass=dnsNode)' -Properties dnsRecord -ResultSetSize 50",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S18:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 17760,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nidentify one exact dnsNode distinguished name, effective create/write-child or record-property right, zone replication scope, resolver path, intended record/value, TTL and cleanup/restore plan. Zone visibility is not write permission.\nACTION PROCEDURE PENDING: discovery/validation only.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S18:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 17320,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nexact writable object/zone and resolver path established → ready for RW10; effective right denied or non-AD-integrated zone → ruled out here; object visible but ACL/replication/client resolver unresolved → inconclusive.\n\n**Verify:** a future write must resolve through the intended client path and cleanup must restore only the changed record. LDAP success alone is insufficient.\n\n[[notes/ad-mapping.md#S18|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S18:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 17709,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nFollow the denied/absent-condition outcome in the linked procedure.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S18:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2280,
      "y": 17906,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nResolve the missing condition; do not infer execution from visibility.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S18:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3130,
      "y": 17320,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Documented checks — action procedure pending\n\n```powershell\n$Root = (Get-ADRootDSE).defaultNamingContext\n  $DnsBase = \"CN=MicrosoftDNS,DC=DomainDnsZones,$Root\"\n  Get-ADObject -SearchBase $DnsBase -LDAPFilter '(objectClass=dnsNode)' -Properties dnsRecord -ResultSetSize 50\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-mapping.md#S18|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
