    {
      "id": "topic:ad-identities",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4740,
      "y": 440,
      "width": 1800,
      "height": 140,
      "text": "# Gain a more useful domain identity\n\nStart from a mapped object/right, an available ticket, or a host whose current privilege may expose a credential source.",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-identities:home",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4740,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 240,
      "text": "## Investigation flow\n\nGain a more useful domain identity\n\n · \n\nBranches describe evidence and missing conditions. Follow one useful lead, then return to unfinished coverage.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-identities:check-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5240,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "## Inspect the tickets/material already available\n\nUse the current identity and ticket cache before attempting credential collection or ticket construction.\n\n```cmd\nklist\n```\n\n**Inventory, convert and import tickets in the correct logon context — on this canvas**"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-identities:check-0-finding-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6290,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### A valid service-scoped ticket\n\nCheck service principal, expiry and the matching client.\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify tickets and use a compatible cache → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-identities:check-0-finding-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6290,
      "y": 845,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### A privileged local token and an accessible credential source\n\nCheck protection and exact source prerequisites before selecting a collector.\n\n**Obtain accessible live logon-session credential material — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-identities:check-0-fallback",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7060,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Unresolved / alternate check\n\nNo useful ticket/source: inspect account configuration and object rights with the available domain identity.\n\n**Enumerate directory objects with native, LDAP and PowerView approaches — on this canvas**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-identities:check-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5240,
      "y": 1274,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "## Choose AS-REP or SPN roasting from account evidence\n\nUse this branch only for a confirmed preauthentication-disabled account; ordinary SPN accounts use a different request.\n\n```bash\nimpacket-GetNPUsers 'DOMAIN/USER' -no-pass -dc-ip DC_IP\n```\n\n**Request AS-REP material for an account without preauthentication — on this canvas**"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-identities:check-1-finding-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6290,
      "y": 1274,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### A valid AS-REP response for the known account\n\nUse the type-specific offline recovery path.\n\n**Request AS-REP material for an account without preauthentication — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-identities:check-1-finding-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6290,
      "y": 1499,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### A normal service account with an SPN\n\nRequest the matching service ticket in an authenticated context.\n\n**Request a selected service ticket for offline service-account recovery — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-identities:check-1-fallback",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7060,
      "y": 1274,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Unresolved / alternate check\n\nThe account requires preauthentication: stop this path and inspect SPNs or effective object rights.\n\n**Validate effective directory-object control — on this canvas**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-identities:check-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5240,
      "y": 1904,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "## Resolve an ACL edge to its concrete operation\n\nUse the exact trustee, target class, GUID and inheritance/deny behavior, not the graph label alone.\n\n```powershell\nGet-DomainObjectAcl -Identity TARGET_OBJECT -ResolveGUIDs\n```\n\n**Validate effective directory-object control — on this canvas**"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-identities:check-2-finding-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6290,
      "y": 1904,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Effective password-reset right on the intended user\n\nConfirm account state and the effect of changing its password.\n\n**Reset a target account password through a validated directory right — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-identities:check-2-finding-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6290,
      "y": 2129,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Effective write to a useful group's member attribute\n\nConfirm the group effect and refresh the resulting token/logon context.\n\n**Add a controlled identity to a group through effective membership rights — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-identities:check-2-finding-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6290,
      "y": 2354,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### WriteOwner/WriteDacl on the target object\n\nPreserve original state and validate each intermediate right.\n\n**Convert ownership or DACL control into a narrower useful right — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:ad-identities:check-2-fallback",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7060,
      "y": 1904,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Unresolved / alternate check\n\nThe right is not effective for the controlled principal: discard that edge and inspect another verified relationship.\n\n**Enumerate directory objects with native, LDAP and PowerView approaches — on this canvas**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "notes:ad-identities",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "notes/ad-identities.md",
      "x": 4740,
      "y": 2764,
      "width": 2100,
      "height": 850
    },
    {
      "id": "notes-label:ad-identities",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7030,
      "y": 2764,
      "width": 1400,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "## Full procedures and alternatives\n\nThe adjacent embedded note is readable here. Scroll inside it for complete variants. Commands and decisions continue below.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-lsass:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 4039,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Obtain accessible live logon-session credential material\n\nA controlled Windows host may hold useful logged-on identities",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-lsass:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 3999,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nwhoami /all\nquery user\nreg query HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa /v RunAsPPL\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-lsass:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 3979,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA useful session is a possible source, while PPL/protection can prevent the chosen process-memory access.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-lsass:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 4225,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify actual privilege, fresh useful sessions, process/architecture compatibility and protection; prefer accessible tickets when sufficient.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-lsass:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 3929,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe authorized source is accessible and yields correctly classified material: follow its actual credential type.\n\n**Verify:** Tie each artifact to an account, source/logon session and material type; independently validate any useful reuse.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-lsass|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-lsass:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 4270,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe required source is protected/unavailable to this context: reject that collection method.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-lsass:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 4491,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA past graph session without fresh host evidence leaves useful live material unknown.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-lsass:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 3929,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```cmd\nwhoami /all\ntasklist /fi \"imagename eq lsass.exe\"\nreg query HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa /v RunAsPPL\nreg query HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa /v LsaCfgFlags\nreg query HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeviceGuard /v LsaCfgFlags\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-lsass|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-lsass:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 4343,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Recover or reuse an NT password hash\n\n**When:** An NT verifier from an appropriate credential source\n\n**Still required:** Correct account/domain and actual NT hash; recovery mode or an accepting NTLM service with required destination rights\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Recover or reuse an NT password hash → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-lsass:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 4650,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Classify tickets and use a compatible cache\n\n**When:** A ccache/kirbi file or an existing ticket cache\n\n**Still required:** Correct principal/realm, valid lifetime, service scope, compatible cache format and naming/KDC route\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify tickets and use a compatible cache → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-lsass:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 4957,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Extract local account hashes from matched SAM and SYSTEM\n\n**When:** Protected local registry material is available under sufficient host privilege\n\n**Still required:** Matched SAM/SYSTEM from the same system and appropriate read/backup access\n\n**Extract local account hashes from matched SAM and SYSTEM — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-lsass:next-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 5288,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Parse an offline domain database or select a justified remote collection path\n\n**When:** An already controlled DC or a validated privileged domain collection context\n\n**Still required:** Matched NTDS/SYSTEM for offline parsing, or the specific remote protocol/host/replication rights required by the chosen method\n\n**Parse an offline domain database or select a justified remote collection path — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-sam:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 5943,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Extract local account hashes from matched SAM and SYSTEM\n\nProtected local registry material is available under sufficient host privilege",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-sam:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 5903,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nhostname\nwhoami /priv\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-sam:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 5883,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nSufficient source access suggests local-account extraction, not domain-account extraction.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-sam:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 6129,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify a supported backup/read operation, complete same-host hives and offline parser context.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-sam:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 6167,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```cmd\nwhoami /priv\nreg save HKLM\\SAM C:\\Windows\\Temp\\SAM.save\nreg save HKLM\\SYSTEM C:\\Windows\\Temp\\SYSTEM.save\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-sam:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 5833,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe matched local pair is available and parses correctly: classify the returned local hashes.\n\n**Verify:** Verify source machine, matched hive pair and account/RID mapping; validate destination rights separately.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-sam|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-sam:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 6174,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nOnly unrelated/mismatched hives are available: reject parsing them as a consistent pair.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-sam:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 6395,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA privilege name alone does not establish the artifacts can be obtained.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-sam:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 5833,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```cmd\nreg save HKLM\\SAM C:\\Windows\\Temp\\SAM.hive /y\nreg save HKLM\\SYSTEM C:\\Windows\\Temp\\SYSTEM.hive /y\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-sam|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-sam:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 6175,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Recover or reuse an NT password hash\n\n**When:** An NT verifier from an appropriate credential source\n\n**Still required:** Correct account/domain and actual NT hash; recovery mode or an accepting NTLM service with required destination rights\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Recover or reuse an NT password hash → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-sam:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 6482,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication\n\n**When:** A password, actual NT hash, AES/NT long-term key or ticket is available\n\n**Still required:** Credential type accepted by the chosen protocol/client, correct identity/domain, naming/time and destination authorization\n\n**Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-sam:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 6813,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Classify the artifact and its identity context\n\n**When:** A secret-like value, key file, stored hash, challenge response or ticket\n\n**Still required:** Artifact provenance and format; possible local/domain/application identity and compatible protocol\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify the artifact and its identity context → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-sam:next-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 7144,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Extract LSA secrets and cached-domain verifiers\n\n**When:** Matched SECURITY/SYSTEM material is accessible\n\n**Still required:** Appropriate host/read privilege and complete matching key/source files\n\n**Extract LSA secrets and cached-domain verifiers — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-security:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 7751,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Extract LSA secrets and cached-domain verifiers\n\nMatched SECURITY/SYSTEM material is accessible",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-security:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 7711,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nhostname\nwhoami /priv\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-security:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 7691,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA SECURITY source targets secrets/cached verifiers with distinct semantics; it is not simply another SAM.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-security:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 7937,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nConfirm matched key material and classify every returned service/machine secret or DCC2 record.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-security:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 7975,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```cmd\nreg save HKLM\\SECURITY C:\\Windows\\Temp\\SECURITY.save\nreg save HKLM\\SYSTEM C:\\Windows\\Temp\\SYSTEM.save\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-security:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 7641,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nA complete matched source yields usable typed material: choose its type-specific next method.\n\n**Verify:** Retain source, account, type and required factors; do not label every parsed output a Pass-the-Hash credential.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-security|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-security:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 7982,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe SYSTEM file comes from another snapshot/machine: reject that consistency assumption.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-security:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 8203,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nAn empty parser result with incomplete source/context leaves credential absence unproved.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-security:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 7641,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```cmd\nreg save HKLM\\SECURITY C:\\Windows\\Temp\\SECURITY.hive /y\nreg save HKLM\\SYSTEM C:\\Windows\\Temp\\SYSTEM.hive /y\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-security|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-security:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 7983,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Recover a password from cached domain logon verifiers\n\n**When:** A DCC2/MSCache record from matched SECURITY/SYSTEM material\n\n**Still required:** Correct username/salt/iteration context and feasible offline candidates\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Recover a password from cached domain logon verifiers → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-security:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 8290,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse\n\n**When:** A password tied to a plausible user and service\n\n**Still required:** Correct local/domain/application identity, reachable compatible service, accepted authentication and account state\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-security:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 8597,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Classify the artifact and its identity context\n\n**When:** A secret-like value, key file, stored hash, challenge response or ticket\n\n**Still required:** Artifact provenance and format; possible local/domain/application identity and compatible protocol\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify the artifact and its identity context → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dpapi:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 9228,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Use Credential Manager and DPAPI with the protecting context\n\nSaved credentials or protected application blobs/master keys",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dpapi:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 9188,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nwhoami /user\ncmdkey /list\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dpapi:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 9168,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe target and protecting SID identify which keys/context or consumer must be investigated.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dpapi:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 9414,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCheck matching master keys/recovery factors or an allowed saved-credential consumer; file read alone is insufficient.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dpapi:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 9452,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```cmd\ncmdkey /list\nwhoami /all\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dpapi:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 9118,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nMatching protection factors decrypt the material or the intended consumer works: use that bounded capability.\n\n**Verify:** Verify the decrypted value or actual saved-credential action in its matching context.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-dpapi|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dpapi:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 9459,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nOnly a blob from an unrelated user is present without its required factors: reject the current decryption route.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dpapi:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 9680,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA cmdkey listing without usable context does not establish a password.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dpapi:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 9118,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```cmd\ncmdkey /list\nvaultcmd /list\nvaultcmd /listcreds:\"Windows Credentials\" /all\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-dpapi|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dpapi:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 9484,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Classify the artifact and its identity context\n\n**When:** A secret-like value, key file, stored hash, challenge response or ticket\n\n**Still required:** Artifact provenance and format; possible local/domain/application identity and compatible protocol\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify the artifact and its identity context → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dpapi:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 9815,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse\n\n**When:** A password tied to a plausible user and service\n\n**Still required:** Correct local/domain/application identity, reachable compatible service, accepted authentication and account state\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dpapi:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 10122,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Recover Windows application, history and stored-credential artifacts\n\n**When:** Readable application configuration, unattended setup, PowerShell trails or Credential Manager entries\n\n**Still required:** Artifact read permission and exact protecting identity/context for saved or DPAPI material\n\n[[tracks/08 Windows Privilege Escalation.canvas|Recover Windows application, history and stored-credential artifacts → 08 Windows Privilege Escalation]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-ntds:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 10753,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Parse an offline domain database or select a justified remote collection path\n\nAn already controlled DC or a validated privileged domain collection context",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-ntds:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 10713,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nfile NTDS.dit SYSTEM.save\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-ntds:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 10693,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA database/key pair is an offline source candidate; remote DRS requires a different permission chain.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-ntds:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 10939,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify same-source consistency and access, or independently validate the exact replication/remote collection prerequisites.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-ntds:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 10643,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe consistent offline pair parses into account-labelled material: choose classification/reuse.\n\n**Verify:** Verify source consistency, account mapping and the exact collection method; retain sensitive output privately.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-ntds|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-ntds:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 10984,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nOnly administrator access on a member server exists: reject the assumed domain-database/replication access.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-ntds:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 11205,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nTwo filenames without provenance do not prove a matched usable source.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-ntds:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 10643,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nimpacket-secretsdump -ntds NTDS.dit -system SYSTEM.hive LOCAL\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-ntds|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-ntds:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 10961,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use validated directory replication rights for bounded credential proof\n\n**When:** A principal has the relevant effective replication rights at the domain naming context\n\n**Still required:** Required replication extended rights, DC RPC connectivity and correct domain identity; access to a member server is insufficient\n\n**Use validated directory replication rights for bounded credential proof — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-ntds:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 11292,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Recover or reuse an NT password hash\n\n**When:** An NT verifier from an appropriate credential source\n\n**Still required:** Correct account/domain and actual NT hash; recovery mode or an accepting NTLM service with required destination rights\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Recover or reuse an NT password hash → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-ntds:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 11599,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Classify the artifact and its identity context\n\n**When:** A secret-like value, key file, stored hash, challenge response or ticket\n\n**Still required:** Artifact provenance and format; possible local/domain/application identity and compatible protocol\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify the artifact and its identity context → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-ntds:next-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 11930,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Conditional: understand a realm-wide TGT forgery from KRBTGT material\n\n**When:** An already compromised domain exposes a KRBTGT key and domain SID\n\n**Still required:** Correct KRBTGT cryptographic material, realm/SID/principal data, valid ticket parameters and compatible service/KDC validation behavior\n\n**Conditional: understand a realm-wide TGT forgery from KRBTGT material — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-asrep:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 12537,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Request AS-REP material for an account without preauthentication\n\nA known user or directory flag indicates Kerberos preauthentication is disabled",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-asrep:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 12497,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nGet-DomainUser -Properties samaccountname,useraccountcontrol |\n  Select-Object samaccountname,@{n='UAC';e={[int]$_.useraccountcontrol}} |\n  Where-Object { ($_.UAC -band 0x400000) -ne 0 }\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-asrep:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 12477,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe DONT_REQUIRE_PREAUTH bit is set. Test the bit, not equality to one whole decimal value, because other flags coexist.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-asrep:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 12723,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCheck account state, KDC route, response/encryption type and feasible recovery; no-password discovery requires a real known username.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-asrep:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 12785,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\nimpacket-GetNPUsers 'DOMAIN/USER' -no-pass -dc-ip DC_IP\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-asrep:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 12427,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe selected enabled account returns the supported AS-REP artifact: choose its offline recovery path.\n\n**Verify:** Verify the account, realm, response format/encryption type and recovered credential if cracking succeeds.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#kerberos-asrep|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-asrep:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 12768,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe KDC requires preauthentication for that account: reject AS-REP roasting for that identity.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-asrep:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 12989,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nAn unknown user or KDC timeout says nothing about the preauthentication setting.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-asrep:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 12427,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```text\nKNOWN USERNAME + PREAUTH DISABLED + KDC REACHABLE\n-> AS-REP CIPHER\n-> OFFLINE GUESSING\n-> PASSWORD ONLY IF A CANDIDATE VERIFIES\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#kerberos-asrep|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-asrep:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 12817,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Recover passwords with feasible dictionary, rule and mask attacks\n\n**When:** A supported stored verifier or converted protected artifact\n\n**Still required:** Correct format/mode, complete salt/context, justified candidates and an available offline tool/backend\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Recover passwords with feasible dictionary, rule and mask attacks → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-asrep:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 13124,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse\n\n**When:** A password tied to a plausible user and service\n\n**Still required:** Correct local/domain/application identity, reachable compatible service, accepted authentication and account state\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-asrep:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 13431,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Request a selected service ticket for offline service-account recovery\n\n**When:** A user-owned SPN and a useful service-account relationship\n\n**Still required:** A valid domain authentication/TGT context, reachable KDC, target SPN and a feasible password/encryption candidate strategy\n\n**Request a selected service ticket for offline service-account recovery — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-roast:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 14038,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Request a selected service ticket for offline service-account recovery\n\nA user-owned SPN and a useful service-account relationship",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-roast:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 13998,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nGet-DomainUser -SPN | Select-Object samaccountname,serviceprincipalname,memberof\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-roast:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 13978,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA user-owned SPN supplies the account key targeted by a service ticket and a reason to assess password-recovery feasibility.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-roast:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 14224,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify valid KDC context, selected account/SPN, returned encryption type, password model and useful resulting rights.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-roast:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 14238,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```bash\nimpacket-GetUserSPNs -dc-ip DC_IP 'DOMAIN/USER:PASSWORD'\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-roast:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 13928,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe selected ticket artifact is supported and recovery is justified: choose the matching offline mode.\n\n**Verify:** Record SPN/account/encryption type and verify any recovered password against the intended identity.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#kerberos-roast|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-roast:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 14269,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe candidate has no SPN and no SPN-write right: reject ordinary/targeted roasting for this account.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-roast:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 14490,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nSPN presence alone leaves weak password and eventual host access unproved.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-roast:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 13928,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```text\nVALID DOMAIN IDENTITY + SPN ACCOUNT + KDC ROUTE\n-> TGS-REP CIPHER\n-> OFFLINE GUESSING\n-> SERVICE-ACCOUNT PASSWORD IF A CANDIDATE VERIFIES\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#kerberos-roast|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-roast:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 14318,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Recover passwords with feasible dictionary, rule and mask attacks\n\n**When:** A supported stored verifier or converted protected artifact\n\n**Still required:** Correct format/mode, complete salt/context, justified candidates and an available offline tool/backend\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Recover passwords with feasible dictionary, rule and mask attacks → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-roast:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 14625,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse\n\n**When:** A password tied to a plausible user and service\n\n**Still required:** Correct local/domain/application identity, reachable compatible service, accepted authentication and account state\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-roast:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 14932,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate host access and volatile session candidates\n\n**When:** Group-to-host access edges or a privileged user's possible session\n\n**Still required:** Reachable destination service and its actual authorization; session evidence must be current and collection rights sufficient\n\n**Validate host access and volatile session candidates — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-targeted-roast:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 15539,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Create a temporary SPN through an effective object right\n\nA controlled principal can write a user's servicePrincipalName",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-targeted-roast:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 15499,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nGet-DomainUser -Identity TARGET_USER -Properties serviceprincipalname\nGet-DomainObjectAcl -Identity TARGET_USER -ResolveGUIDs\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-targeted-roast:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 15479,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA specific writable SPN property on a useful user can create a ticket-request opportunity.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-targeted-roast:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 15725,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify trustee/effective property scope, enabled account, unique temporary SPN, KDC context and exact restoration.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-targeted-roast:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 15763,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```powershell\nGet-DomainObjectAcl -Identity TARGET_USER -ResolveGUIDs\nsetspn -L TARGET_USER\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-targeted-roast:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 15429,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe permitted temporary SPN produces the selected artifact and is removed: use the targeted recovery method.\n\n**Verify:** Verify effective right, requested account and cleanup; confirm any recovered credential independently.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-targeted-roast|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-targeted-roast:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 15770,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe ACE does not apply to this property/object: reject the proposed SPN modification.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-targeted-roast:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 15991,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA stale GenericWrite graph edge without current ACE verification is insufficient.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-targeted-roast:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 15429,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```cmd\nsetspn -L TARGET_USER\nsetspn -S temporary/TARGET_USER TARGET_USER\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-targeted-roast|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-targeted-roast:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 15771,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Recover passwords with feasible dictionary, rule and mask attacks\n\n**When:** A supported stored verifier or converted protected artifact\n\n**Still required:** Correct format/mode, complete salt/context, justified candidates and an available offline tool/backend\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Recover passwords with feasible dictionary, rule and mask attacks → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-targeted-roast:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 16078,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse\n\n**When:** A password tied to a plausible user and service\n\n**Still required:** Correct local/domain/application identity, reachable compatible service, accepted authentication and account state\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-targeted-roast:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 16385,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Validate effective directory-object control\n\n**When:** An ACL/graph edge names GenericAll, GenericWrite, WriteDacl, WriteOwner or an extended/property right\n\n**Still required:** Effective trustee membership, target object/type, inheritance/deny behavior and the exact permitted operation\n\n**Validate effective directory-object control — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-tickets:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 17016,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Inventory, convert and import tickets in the correct logon context\n\nA valid ticket/cache or a long-term key that can request a TGT",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-tickets:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 16976,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nklist\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-tickets:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 16956,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA current TGT can request appropriate service tickets if the KDC/name route and account context work.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-tickets:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 17202,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nDistinguish TGT from TGS, format, logon-session scope, lifetime, SPN and destination authorization.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-tickets:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 16906,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe matching service accepts the selected ticket context: choose that scoped operation.\n\n**Verify:** Verify ticket client/server/lifetime and an actual service operation; record local versus network identity separately.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#kerberos-tickets|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-tickets:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 17247,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nOnly an unrelated expired service ticket exists: reject it for the proposed destination.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-tickets:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 17468,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nSuccessful import with no service action leaves usable access unproved.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-tickets:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 16906,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 372,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```cmd\nklist\nklist tgt\nklist sessions\nklist -li 0xLUID tickets\nklist -li 0xLUID tgt\nRubeus.exe triage\nRubeus.exe dump /luid:0xLUID /nowrap\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#kerberos-tickets|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-tickets:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 17368,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication\n\n**When:** A password, actual NT hash, AES/NT long-term key or ticket is available\n\n**Still required:** Credential type accepted by the chosen protocol/client, correct identity/domain, naming/time and destination authorization\n\n**Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-tickets:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 17699,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Execute through uploaded service creation using PsExec\n\n**When:** A destination grants administrative-share write and service-control rights\n\n**Still required:** SMB/SCM reachability, writable required share, effective service-creation/start rights and an accepted password/hash or supported Kerberos context\n\n**Execute through uploaded service creation using PsExec — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-tickets:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 18054,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Preserve DNS, Kerberos names and time across a pivot\n\n**When:** An IP connection works while hostname/Kerberos access fails\n\n**Still required:** Reachable correct resolver/KDC path, matching target SPN/hostname, realm configuration and acceptable time\n\n[[tracks/10 Pivoting.canvas|Preserve DNS, Kerberos names and time across a pivot → 10 Pivoting]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-tickets:next-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 18361,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Forge a service-scoped ticket from the correct service key\n\n**When:** A service account key and a concrete compatible service/SPN objective\n\n**Still required:** Correct service key/encryption type, domain SID, principal/SPN data and service validation behavior; modern PAC/KDC validation can constrain use\n\n**Forge a service-scoped ticket from the correct service key — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-silver:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 19016,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Forge a service-scoped ticket from the correct service key\n\nA service account key and a concrete compatible service/SPN objective",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-silver:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 18976,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nsetspn -Q SERVICE/TARGET_HOST\nwhoami /user\nklist\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-silver:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 18956,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe key must protect the intended service ticket; an arbitrary user's NT hash is not sufficient.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-silver:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 19202,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify key type/current value, domain SID, principal/SPN, validation behavior and accepted target action.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-silver:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 19264,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```cmd\nwhoami /user\nklist\nsetspn -Q SERVICE/TARGET_HOST\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-silver:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 18906,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nA correctly scoped ticket is accepted by the intended service: use only that verified service effect.\n\n**Verify:** Prove the intended service action and ticket context; ticket creation/import success alone is insufficient.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#kerberos-silver|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-silver:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 19247,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe key belongs to a different account/SPN or is outdated: reject the forgery.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-silver:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 19468,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nTicket creation alone does not settle modern PAC/service validation.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-silver:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 18906,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nimpacket-ticketer -nthash SERVICE_NT_HASH -domain-sid DOMAIN_SID \\\n  -domain DOMAIN -spn cifs/TARGET_HOST AUTHORIZED_TEST_USER\nexport KRB5CCNAME=\"$PWD/AUTHORIZED_TEST_USER.ccache\"\nklist\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#kerberos-silver|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-silver:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 19296,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication\n\n**When:** A password, actual NT hash, AES/NT long-term key or ticket is available\n\n**Still required:** Credential type accepted by the chosen protocol/client, correct identity/domain, naming/time and destination authorization\n\n**Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-silver:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 19627,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Enumerate SMB/RPC shares, files and identities\n\n**When:** SMB/RPC endpoints, domain clues or new credentials\n\n**Still required:** Reachable SMB/RPC; anonymous, guest, local or domain context must be explicit; share and filesystem ACLs both matter\n\n[[tracks/02 Services.canvas|Enumerate SMB/RPC shares, files and identities → 02 Services]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-silver:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 19934,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Classify the artifact and its identity context\n\n**When:** A secret-like value, key file, stored hash, challenge response or ticket\n\n**Still required:** Artifact provenance and format; possible local/domain/application identity and compatible protocol\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify the artifact and its identity context → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-password-reset:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 20565,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Reset a target account password through a validated directory right\n\nA controlled trustee has the effective password-reset right on a useful account",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-password-reset:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 20525,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nGet-DomainObjectAcl -Identity TARGET_USER -ResolveGUIDs\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-password-reset:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 20505,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nAn applicable reset operation changes a target credential; it does not reveal the old password.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-password-reset:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 20751,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nValidate effective membership, protection/account state, account utility and the authorized impact of a disruptive reset.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-password-reset:checks",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 20765,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Validate the condition\n\n```powershell\nGet-DomainObjectAcl -Identity TARGET_USER -ResolveGUIDs\nGet-DomainUser -Identity TARGET_USER\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-password-reset:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 20455,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe right applies and the authorized new credential is accepted: follow that identity's actual rights.\n\n**Verify:** Verify account identity and compatible authentication, then test relevant authorization.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-password-reset|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-password-reset:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 20796,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nOnly an unrelated property-write right applies: reject password reset through this ACE.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-password-reset:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 21017,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nAn unresolved extended-right GUID or stale group edge needs effective-right resolution first.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-password-reset:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 20455,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```powershell\n$Secure = ConvertTo-SecureString 'TEMP_PASSWORD' -AsPlainText -Force\nSet-DomainUserPassword -Identity TARGET_USER -AccountPassword $Secure -Verbose\nnet user TARGET_USER TEMP_PASSWORD /domain\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-password-reset|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-password-reset:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 20821,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse\n\n**When:** A password tied to a plausible user and service\n\n**Still required:** Correct local/domain/application identity, reachable compatible service, accepted authentication and account state\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-password-reset:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 21128,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate host access and volatile session candidates\n\n**When:** Group-to-host access edges or a privileged user's possible session\n\n**Still required:** Reachable destination service and its actual authorization; session evidence must be current and collection rights sufficient\n\n**Validate host access and volatile session candidates — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-password-reset:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 21435,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Match route, destination service and effective authorization\n\n**When:** A credential appears valid but the destination's usable access is unknown\n\n**Still required:** Real source-to-service route, correct identity context and protocol-specific execution/logon rights\n\n**Match route, destination service and effective authorization — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-group-control:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 22066,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Add a controlled identity to a group through effective membership rights\n\nA group member-attribute write or equivalent effective right",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-group-control:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 22026,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nGet-DomainGroupMember -Identity TARGET_GROUP\nGet-DomainObjectAcl -Identity TARGET_GROUP -ResolveGUIDs\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-group-control:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 22006,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA membership-write operation can grant a defined group capability once new logon/token state reflects it.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-group-control:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 22252,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify effective right, actual group-derived authorization, nesting/token refresh and restoration.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-group-control:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 21956,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe membership and a fresh context enable the intended service action: choose the group transition.\n\n**Verify:** Verify directory membership and actual service action from a refreshed context, then restore the original membership.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-group-control|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-group-control:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 22297,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe writable attribute is not member or the group grants no intended right: reject that chain.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-group-control:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 22518,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nDirectory modification without refreshed/accepted authorization leaves practical effect unresolved.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-group-control:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 21956,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 348,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```powershell\nAdd-DomainGroupMember -Identity TARGET_GROUP -Members CONTROLLED_USER -Verbose\nGet-DomainGroupMember -Identity TARGET_GROUP |\n  Where-Object { $_.MemberName -eq 'CONTROLLED_USER' }\n\n# Built-in alternative\nnet group TARGET_GROUP CONTROLLED_USER /add /domain\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-group-control|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-group-control:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 22394,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use WinRM, WinRS or PowerShell remoting\n\n**When:** A WinRM listener and a candidate endpoint-authorized account\n\n**Still required:** Reachable HTTP(S) listener, accepted authentication and endpoint/session configuration permissions; hash/ticket support depends on client/context\n\n**Use WinRM, WinRS or PowerShell remoting — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-group-control:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 22725,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate host access and volatile session candidates\n\n**When:** Group-to-host access edges or a privileged user's possible session\n\n**Still required:** Reachable destination service and its actual authorization; session evidence must be current and collection rights sufficient\n\n**Validate host access and volatile session candidates — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-group-control:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 23032,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse\n\n**When:** A password tied to a plausible user and service\n\n**Still required:** Correct local/domain/application identity, reachable compatible service, accepted authentication and account state\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Validate known passwords and context-specific reuse → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-owner-dacl:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 23639,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Convert ownership or DACL control into a narrower useful right\n\nEffective WriteOwner or WriteDacl on a useful directory object",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-owner-dacl:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 23599,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nGet-DomainObjectAcl -Identity TARGET_OBJECT -ResolveGUIDs\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-owner-dacl:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 23579,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nOwnership/DACL control may enable a narrower useful ACE; it is an intermediate capability.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-owner-dacl:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 23825,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nValidate actual owner semantics, deny/protected-object behavior, ability to grant the next right and original-state restoration.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-owner-dacl:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 23529,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe intermediate operation and narrow effective right are established: follow the linked reset/group/SPN method.\n\n**Verify:** Verify the intermediate owner/DACL state and final operation separately; restore original state afterward.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-owner-dacl|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-owner-dacl:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 23870,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe ACE targets another object scope or is ineffective for this trustee: reject that route.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-owner-dacl:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 24091,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nWriteOwner text alone does not prove every later DACL modification succeeds.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-owner-dacl:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 23529,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 468,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```powershell\nSet-DomainObjectOwner -Identity TARGET_OBJECT -OwnerIdentity CONTROLLED_USER -Verbose\nAdd-DomainObjectAcl -TargetIdentity TARGET_OBJECT -PrincipalIdentity CONTROLLED_USER -Rights ResetPassword -Verbose\n\n# Group-membership variant\nAdd-DomainObjectAcl -TargetIdentity TARGET_GROUP -PrincipalIdentity CONTROLLED_USER -Rights WriteMembers -Verbose\n\n# Remove the ACE after the authorized objective\nRemove-DomainObjectAcl -TargetIdentity TARGET_OBJECT -PrincipalIdentity CONTROLLED_USER -Rights ResetPassword -Verbose\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-owner-dacl|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-owner-dacl:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 24087,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Reset a target account password through a validated directory right\n\n**When:** A controlled trustee has the effective password-reset right on a useful account\n\n**Still required:** Exact object/right and account state; the disruptive password change is justified within the assigned lab objective\n\n**Reset a target account password through a validated directory right — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-owner-dacl:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 24418,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Add a controlled identity to a group through effective membership rights\n\n**When:** A group member-attribute write or equivalent effective right\n\n**Still required:** Exact target group, controlled principal, useful resulting right and a fresh token/logon context\n\n**Add a controlled identity to a group through effective membership rights — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-owner-dacl:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 24725,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Create a temporary SPN through an effective object right\n\n**When:** A controlled principal can write a user's servicePrincipalName\n\n**Still required:** Effective SPN-property right, compatible account, unique temporary SPN, authenticated TGS request and exact cleanup\n\n**Create a temporary SPN through an effective object right — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dcsync:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 25332,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Use validated directory replication rights for bounded credential proof\n\nA principal has the relevant effective replication rights at the domain naming context",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dcsync:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 25292,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nGet-DomainObjectAcl -Identity DOMAIN_DN -ResolveGUIDs\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dcsync:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 25272,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nReplication rights at the domain scope are the relevant clue; local administrator rights on a member host are different.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dcsync:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 25518,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify the complete effective replication rights for selected data, trustee membership, DC/RPC route and identity context.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dcsync:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 25222,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe required rights and route produce the bounded selected-account proof: choose DRS replication.\n\n**Verify:** Verify the replication source, account and material type; avoid equating a tool label with proven rights.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-dcsync|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dcsync:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 25563,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe ACE applies only to a user/OU or lacks required replication rights: reject DCSync.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dcsync:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 25784,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nUnresolved GUIDs or RPC filtering leave rights/access separately unknown.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dcsync:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 25222,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```powershell\nGet-DomainObjectAcl -Identity 'DC=DOMAIN,DC=TLD' -ResolveGUIDs |\n  Where-Object { $_.ObjectAceType -match 'Replication-Get-Changes' }\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-dcsync|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dcsync:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 25564,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Recover or reuse an NT password hash\n\n**When:** An NT verifier from an appropriate credential source\n\n**Still required:** Correct account/domain and actual NT hash; recovery mode or an accepting NTLM service with required destination rights\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Recover or reuse an NT password hash → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dcsync:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 25871,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Inventory, convert and import tickets in the correct logon context\n\n**When:** A valid ticket/cache or a long-term key that can request a TGT\n\n**Still required:** Matching client/realm/service, valid lifetime, compatible format and available KDC/service routes; ticket import affects a specific context\n\n**Inventory, convert and import tickets in the correct logon context — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-dcsync:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 26202,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Capture state-transition, proof and exploit-adaptation evidence\n\n**When:** Access, privilege, identity or route changes, or a report will need reproduction\n\n**Still required:** Known destination/identity, observable effect and a private evidence destination; actual exam proof requirements must be read from current official guidance\n\n[[tracks/12 Evidence and Reporting.canvas|Capture state-transition, proof and exploit-adaptation evidence → 12 Evidence and Reporting]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-gpo:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 26857,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Conditional: trace GPO control to privileged policy consumption\n\nA useful linked GPO has a potentially controllable directory or SYSVOL component",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-gpo:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 26817,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nGet-DomainGPO\nGet-DomainOU | Select-Object name,gplink\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-gpo:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 26797,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA linked policy supplies a potential privileged consumer only for hosts to which it actually applies.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-gpo:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 27043,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCheck both needed policy components, effective ACEs, security/WMI filtering, target scope and refresh trigger.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-gpo:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 26747,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe controlled policy is consumed on the intended host and effect verified: choose this conditional route.\n\n**Verify:** Verify actual policy application and resulting privileged effect; retain/restorable original policy state.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-gpo|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-gpo:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 27088,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe target is excluded by policy filtering: reject that policy-to-host chain.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-gpo:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 27285,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA writable GPO object without linked/applicable file-consumer evidence remains incomplete.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-gpo:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 26747,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```powershell\nGet-DomainGPO\nGet-DomainOU | Select-Object name,distinguishedname,gplink\nGet-DomainObjectAcl -SearchBase 'CN=Policies,CN=System,DC=DOMAIN,DC=TLD' -ResolveGUIDs |\n  Where-Object { $_.ActiveDirectoryRights -match 'GenericAll|GenericWrite|WriteDacl|WriteProperty' }\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-gpo|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-gpo:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 27137,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Validate effective directory-object control\n\n**When:** An ACL/graph edge names GenericAll, GenericWrite, WriteDacl, WriteOwner or an extended/property right\n\n**Still required:** Effective trustee membership, target object/type, inheritance/deny behavior and the exact permitted operation\n\n**Validate effective directory-object control — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-gpo:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 27468,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Control scheduled tasks, startup files or autostart consumers\n\n**When:** A task/startup action consumes a writable command, file, directory or registry value\n\n**Still required:** Effective object control, a higher principal and a usable scheduled/logon/manual trigger\n\n[[tracks/08 Windows Privilege Escalation.canvas|Control scheduled tasks, startup files or autostart consumers → 08 Windows Privilege Escalation]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-gpo:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 27799,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Maintain state and select the next evidence-producing test\n\n**When:** Several hosts, identities, routes or competing hypotheses need coordination\n\n**Still required:** Explicit scope/objective and a record of observations, unknowns and available capabilities\n\n[[tracks/12 Evidence and Reporting.canvas|Maintain state and select the next evidence-producing test → 12 Evidence and Reporting]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-delegation:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 28430,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Conditional: use a validated delegation or RBCD relationship\n\nDelegation configuration or computer-object write suggests a Kerberos impersonation path",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-delegation:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 28390,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nGet-DomainComputer -TrustedToAuth\nGet-DomainComputer -Unconstrained\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-delegation:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 28370,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA delegation flag opens a configuration investigation; unconstrained, constrained and RBCD require different relationships.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-delegation:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 28616,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nIdentify exact delegation type, controlled service/machine key, target SPN, relevant account flags and KDC acceptance.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-delegation:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 28320,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe complete matching relationship yields an accepted service ticket: use that service-scoped conditional path.\n\n**Verify:** Verify the exact service ticket and successful destination action, with original delegation state preserved.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-delegation|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-delegation:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 28661,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe required service identity/key or allowed target is missing: reject that chain.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-delegation:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 28882,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA generic delegation label without actual attributes/keys leaves impersonation unproved.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-delegation:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 28320,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```powershell\nGet-DomainComputer -Unconstrained | Select-Object dnshostname\nGet-DomainUser -TrustedToAuth | Select-Object samaccountname\nGet-DomainComputer -TrustedToAuth | Select-Object dnshostname\nGet-DomainObject -LDAPFilter '(msDS-AllowedToDelegateTo=*)' -Properties samaccountname,msds-allowedtodelegateto\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-delegation|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-delegation:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 28710,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Inventory, convert and import tickets in the correct logon context\n\n**When:** A valid ticket/cache or a long-term key that can request a TGT\n\n**Still required:** Matching client/realm/service, valid lifetime, compatible format and available KDC/service routes; ticket import affects a specific context\n\n**Inventory, convert and import tickets in the correct logon context — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-delegation:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 29041,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication\n\n**When:** A password, actual NT hash, AES/NT long-term key or ticket is available\n\n**Still required:** Credential type accepted by the chosen protocol/client, correct identity/domain, naming/time and destination authorization\n\n**Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-delegation:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 29372,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Validate effective directory-object control\n\n**When:** An ACL/graph edge names GenericAll, GenericWrite, WriteDacl, WriteOwner or an extended/property right\n\n**Still required:** Effective trustee membership, target object/type, inheritance/deny behavior and the exact permitted operation\n\n**Validate effective directory-object control — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-certificates:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 30003,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Conditional: validate an AD CS enrollment-to-authentication path\n\nA CA/template configuration exposes a plausible certificate identity transition",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-certificates:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 29963,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\ncertipy find -u 'USER@DOMAIN' -p 'PASSWORD' -dc-ip DC_IP -enabled\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-certificates:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 29943,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe conjunction of purpose, subject control and effective enrollment rights is a candidate; issuance and identity mapping are separate gates.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-certificates:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 30189,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCheck exact template/CA rights/settings, approval/signatures, required key, current mapping and authenticatable identity.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-certificates:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 29893,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nIssuance and intended account authentication are verified: use the certificate capability.\n\n**Verify:** Verify issuance, matching private key, mapped account and a successful authentication effect; preserve and restore template changes.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-certificates|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-certificates:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 30234,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nApproval, denied enrollment or hardened mapping prevents the proposed transition: reject that route.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-certificates:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 30455,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nAn ESC scanner label without the full effective configuration remains unconfirmed.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-certificates:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 29893,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\ncommand -v certipy-ad || command -v certipy\ncertipy-ad find -u 'USER@DOMAIN' -p 'PASSWORD' -dc-ip DC_IP \\\n  -enabled -vulnerable -stdout\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#ad-certificates|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-certificates:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 30259,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Classify the artifact and its identity context\n\n**When:** A secret-like value, key file, stored hash, challenge response or ticket\n\n**Still required:** Artifact provenance and format; possible local/domain/application identity and compatible protocol\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify the artifact and its identity context → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-certificates:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 30590,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Inventory, convert and import tickets in the correct logon context\n\n**When:** A valid ticket/cache or a long-term key that can request a TGT\n\n**Still required:** Matching client/realm/service, valid lifetime, compatible format and available KDC/service routes; ticket import affects a specific context\n\n**Inventory, convert and import tickets in the correct logon context — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:ad-certificates:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 30921,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Validate effective directory-object control\n\n**When:** An ACL/graph edge names GenericAll, GenericWrite, WriteDacl, WriteOwner or an extended/property right\n\n**Still required:** Effective trustee membership, target object/type, inheritance/deny behavior and the exact permitted operation\n\n**Validate effective directory-object control — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-golden:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 31552,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Conditional: understand a realm-wide TGT forgery from KRBTGT material\n\nAn already compromised domain exposes a KRBTGT key and domain SID",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-golden:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 31512,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nklist\nwhoami /user\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-golden:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 31492,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nKRBTGT key exposure is the enabling post-compromise condition; an ordinary NT hash or unrelated ticket cannot substitute.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-golden:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 31738,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify current cryptographic material/version, realm/SID/principal, time and actual service validation; retain recovery/cleanup scope.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-golden:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 31442,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe authorized isolated-lab ticket is accepted for the intended action: document the domain-key impact.\n\n**Verify:** Verify cryptographic source, represented principal and exact service effect; protect the key and remove generated test credentials.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#kerberos-golden|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-golden:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 31783,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nOnly an ordinary service-account key is available: reject realm-wide TGT forgery.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-golden:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 32004,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA file labelled KRBTGT without source/version verification leaves the key claim unresolved.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-golden:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 31442,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 348,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\n# Golden: realm-wide TGT material\nimpacket-ticketer -nthash KRBTGT_NT_HASH -domain-sid DOMAIN_SID \\\n  -domain DOMAIN AUTHORIZED_TEST_USER\n\nexport KRB5CCNAME=\"$PWD/AUTHORIZED_TEST_USER.ccache\"\nklist\n```\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#kerberos-golden|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-golden:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 31880,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Inventory, convert and import tickets in the correct logon context\n\n**When:** A valid ticket/cache or a long-term key that can request a TGT\n\n**Still required:** Matching client/realm/service, valid lifetime, compatible format and available KDC/service routes; ticket import affects a specific context\n\n**Inventory, convert and import tickets in the correct logon context — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-golden:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 32211,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication\n\n**When:** A password, actual NT hash, AES/NT long-term key or ticket is available\n\n**Still required:** Credential type accepted by the chosen protocol/client, correct identity/domain, naming/time and destination authorization\n\n**Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:kerberos-golden:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 7810,
      "y": 32542,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Capture state-transition, proof and exploit-adaptation evidence\n\n**When:** Access, privilege, identity or route changes, or a report will need reproduction\n\n**Still required:** Known destination/identity, observable effect and a private evidence destination; actual exam proof requirements must be read from current official guidance\n\n[[tracks/12 Evidence and Reporting.canvas|Capture state-transition, proof and exploit-adaptation evidence → 12 Evidence and Reporting]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S02:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 33197,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Read a classic LAPS password for one computer\n\na specific computer object is relevant and the current directory principal may read ms-Mcs-AdmPwd.",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S02:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 33157,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nSee the linked discovery procedure.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S02:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 33137,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nidentify the computer object and test the attribute read; merely enumerating the object is not enough.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S02:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 33383,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nthe returned value is present, current and scoped to that computer's managed local account; identify the intended local username and destination service separately.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S02:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 33087,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nreadable current value → D17/D29; attribute denied/absent for this principal/object → ruled out here; schema, replication freshness or object identity unresolved → inconclusive.\n\n**Verify:** validate the password on one compatible service using explicit local-account context, then prove the specific permitted operation. Password acceptance does not prove local administration or remote execution.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#S02|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S02:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 33476,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nFollow the denied/absent-condition outcome in the linked procedure.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S02:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 33673,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nResolve the missing condition; do not infer execution from visibility.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S03:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 34160,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Read or decrypt a Windows LAPS password\n\na relevant computer uses Windows LAPS and the principal may read msLAPS-Password or decrypt the protected value.",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S03:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 34120,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nSee the linked discovery procedure.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S03:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 34100,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nquery the exact computer attribute and record whether the result is plaintext JSON, encrypted content, empty or denied.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S03:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 34346,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nplaintext/decryption rights, password age, managed account name and host scope. An encrypted blob without the permitted decryption context is not a password.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S03:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 34050,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nusable current password → D17/D29; no read/decrypt right → ruled out here; returned protected data but decryption context unknown → inconclusive.\n\n**Verify:** validate only against the named host and intended local account, then establish the actual service capability.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#S03|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S03:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 34391,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nFollow the denied/absent-condition outcome in the linked procedure.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S03:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 34588,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nResolve the missing condition; do not infer execution from visibility.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S04:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 35075,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Recover and classify gMSA material\n\na specific gMSA is used by a relevant service and the current identity may read msDS-ManagedPassword.",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S04:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 35035,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nSee the linked discovery procedure.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S04:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 35015,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\ninspect the gMSA object and allowed managed-password readers; distinguish a raw blob from a decoded NT hash.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S04:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 35261,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nexact account name including $, managed-password read permission, working LDAPS/tool path, decoded representation and intended service/host.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S04:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 34965,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\ndecoded material accepted for the intended identity → D17/D29; read denied or wrong object type → ruled out here; raw blob, TLS failure or empty output → inconclusive.\n\n**Verify:** test one service compatible with the decoded material and record the exact accepted identity and operation. Authentication is not administrative execution.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#S04|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S04:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 35354,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nFollow the denied/absent-condition outcome in the linked procedure.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S04:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 35551,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nResolve the missing condition; do not infer execution from visibility.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S05:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 36038,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Use a validated shadow-credential path\n\nthe effective principal can write the target object's msDS-KeyCredentialLink, and the assigned lab permits the object change.",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S05:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 35998,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nSee the linked discovery procedure.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S05:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 35978,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nlist existing key credentials before mutation and preserve their identifiers.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S05:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 36224,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\ntarget identity, exact effective write right, DC PKINIT/key-trust support, DNS/time/KDC route, certificate tooling and a cleanup route.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S05:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 35928,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\ntarget TGT/service capability established → D28/D29; effective write or PKINIT prerequisite disproved → ruled out here; write succeeds but certificate/KDC mapping is unresolved → D31/inconclusive.\n\n**Verify:** establish the cached target principal and one intended service action; then confirm that only the newly added key credential was removed.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#S05|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S05:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 36293,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nFollow the denied/absent-condition outcome in the linked procedure.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S05:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 36490,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nResolve the missing condition; do not infer execution from visibility.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S06:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 36977,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Authenticate to LDAP with a mapped certificate\n\nyou possess a certificate and private key plausibly mapped to an AD identity, and LDAP over TLS is reachable.",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S06:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 36937,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nSee the linked discovery procedure.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S06:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 36917,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nidentify certificate subject/SAN/EKU, trust chain, private-key availability and the DC TLS path.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S06:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 37163,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nthe certificate maps to the intended principal, the private key matches, Schannel authentication is accepted and the mapped identity has the exact object right required by the intended LDAP operation.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S06:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 36867,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nmapped identity and permitted object operation confirmed → D26; mapping/trust/private key disproved → ruled out here; PKINIT fails while Schannel remains untested, or TLS errors mask mapping → inconclusive.\n\n**Verify:** whoami/bind establishes only the mapped LDAP identity; separately verify the selected LDAP read or write and its object state.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#S06|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S06:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 37232,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nFollow the denied/absent-condition outcome in the linked procedure.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S06:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 37429,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nResolve the missing condition; do not infer execution from visibility.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S07:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 37916,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Create a controlled machine account only for a selected AD path\n\na validated RBCD/delegation path needs a service principal or machine key you control.",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S07:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 37876,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nSee the linked discovery procedure.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S07:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 37856,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\ninspect machine-account quota, target OU/container ACL, existing names and whether the current identity can create the account in the intended location.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S07:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 38126,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nthe downstream path actually needs this principal, the resulting SPNs/key will be usable, target-object rights are independently present, and cleanup/deletion rights are understood.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S07:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 37806,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\ncontrolled principal created for an already validated receiver path → D27; quota/ACL/name condition fails → ruled out here; object exists but downstream target right is missing → retain only the machine-account capability.\n\n**Verify:** confirm the created object, its SPNs and controlled key; do not record RBCD or target access until the separate delegation operation and service ticket succeed.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#S07|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S07:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 38195,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nFollow the denied/absent-condition outcome in the linked procedure.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S07:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 38392,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nResolve the missing condition; do not infer execution from visibility.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S08:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 38879,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Evaluate DNSAdmins without assuming immediate execution\n\nthe controlled principal is a direct/effective DNSAdmins member or has equivalent DNS-server configuration rights.",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S08:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 38839,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nSee the linked discovery procedure.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S08:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 38819,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nidentify the actual DNS server, DNS service state/identity and service ACL from the current authorized source.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S08:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 39065,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\neffective configuration permission, product/build behavior, a usable plugin/configuration operation, payload delivery path and a separately authorized restart trigger. A restart on a DC is disruptive and is never a discovery probe.\nACTION PROCEDURE PENDING: discovery/validation only.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S08:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 38769,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nall prerequisites identified → ready for a separately reviewed procedure; membership absent/effective right denied → ruled out here; group present but configuration or trigger unknown → inconclusive.\n\n**Verify:** current content supports only membership/service/trigger investigation. A complete plugin execution and cleanup procedure is not registered; see RW01.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#S08|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S08:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 39158,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nFollow the denied/absent-condition outcome in the linked procedure.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S08:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 39355,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nResolve the missing condition; do not infer execution from visibility.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S09:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 39842,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Map WSUS client policy to a server-side authorization question\n\nhost policy or traffic indicates the machine uses WSUS.",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S09:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 39802,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nSee the linked discovery procedure.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S09:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 39782,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nread WUServer, WUStatusServer and UseWUServer; record URL, port, TLS and actual source reachability.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S09:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 40028,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nauthenticated access to the identified server, update-approval/content/signing/deployment rights, target group scope and the privileged client consumer. Client configuration alone supplies none of those rights.\nACTION PROCEDURE PENDING: discovery/validation only.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S09:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 39732,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nauthority plus exact server-side control established → ready for a separately reviewed procedure; server rights denied → ruled out here; registry values absent or server role unknown → inconclusive.\n\n**Verify:** this state produces a named update authority and a missing-rights checklist, not code execution. A complete update-deployment procedure is not registered; see RW02.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#S09|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S09:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 40121,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nFollow the denied/absent-condition outcome in the linked procedure.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S09:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 40318,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nResolve the missing condition; do not infer execution from visibility.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S10:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 40805,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Recognize SCCM client context and locate the management boundary\n\nCcmExec, SMS_Client or readable client configuration indicates Configuration Manager.",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S10:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 40765,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nSee the linked discovery procedure.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S10:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 40745,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nidentify client state, assigned site, management point and reachable authenticated interfaces.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S10:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 40991,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nSMS Provider/site-server authorization, deployment or CMPivot rights, relevant collection scope and any specifically readable credential source. Client presence does not imply server rights.\nACTION PROCEDURE PENDING: discovery/validation only.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S10:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 40695,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nexact management interface and relevant permission found → ready for a separately reviewed procedure; no applicable server permission → ruled out here; namespace access denied or site/role unresolved → inconclusive.\n\n**Verify:** this state establishes product/site context only. A complete SCCM rights-to-action procedure is not registered; see RW03.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#S10|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S10:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 41060,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nFollow the denied/absent-condition outcome in the linked procedure.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S10:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 41257,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nResolve the missing condition; do not infer execution from visibility.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S16:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 41744,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Inspect VSS/shadow-copy credential-source conditions\n\nyou control a Windows Server/DC context where offline credential material is relevant and the token may hold administrative or backup rights.",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S16:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 41704,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nSee the linked discovery procedure.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S16:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 41684,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\ninspect whoami /priv, vssadmin list shadows, then diskshadow → list shadows all.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S16:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 41930,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nestablish platform, exact volume, existing-versus-new snapshot, read rights, matched NTDS.dit and SYSTEM-hive requirement, output destination and cleanup authority.\nACTION PROCEDURE PENDING: discovery/validation only.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S16:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 41634,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nsuitable existing snapshot and read path identified → ready for RW08 procedure; platform/rights/volume/source decisively incompatible → ruled out here; snapshot listed but access/freshness/matching hive unresolved → inconclusive.\n\n**Verify:** listing proves only snapshot metadata. Credential acquisition requires readable, point-in-time-compatible NTDS/SYSTEM material and successful offline parsing.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#S16|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S16:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 42023,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nFollow the denied/absent-condition outcome in the linked procedure.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S16:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 42220,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nResolve the missing condition; do not infer execution from visibility.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S19:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4750,
      "y": 42707,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Separate an unconstrained-delegation flag from tickets actually present\n\na computer/service account has TrustedForDelegation/unconstrained delegation and the selected host/session context is accessible.",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S19:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 5250,
      "y": 42667,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nSee the linked discovery procedure.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S19:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 42647,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nconfirm the account/SPNs and inspect the actual selected ticket cache with klist or Rubeus.exe triage in the permitted context.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S19:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6180,
      "y": 42893,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nticket owner, realm, service/TGT type, validity, logon-session/LUID access, export/cache compatibility and the exact receiving service. A delegation flag without a cached client ticket is only configuration.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S19:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 42597,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nusable cached ticket accepted by the named service → D28/D29; no relevant ticket in the inspectable context → current cached-ticket path ruled out; inaccessible LUID, stale ticket or ambiguous principal → inconclusive.\n\n**Verify:** prove one named service action under the ticket principal, then preserve the host/LUID/cache scope. Do not record a password, hash or domain-wide privilege.\n\n[[notes/ad-identities.md#S19|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S19:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 42986,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nFollow the denied/absent-condition outcome in the linked procedure.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S19:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6960,
      "y": 43183,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nResolve the missing condition; do not infer execution from visibility.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "topic-group:lateral-movement",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 9360,
      "y": 420,
      "width": 4400,
      "height": 18769,
      "label": "Move to another host",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:move-preflight",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 9395,
      "y": 2985,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 2441,
      "label": "Match route, destination service and effective authorization",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:move-services",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 9395,
      "y": 5551,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1448,
      "label": "Execute through uploaded service creation using PsExec",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:move-smbexec",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 9395,
      "y": 7124,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1400,
      "label": "Execute commands through service command lines and SMB output",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:move-tasks",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 9395,
      "y": 8649,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1352,
      "label": "Execute through remote Task Scheduler",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:move-wmi",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 9395,
      "y": 10126,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1376,
      "label": "Execute through WMI or native CIM over DCOM",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:move-dcom",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 9395,
      "y": 11627,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1496,
      "label": "Execute through an authorized DCOM application object",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:move-winrm",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 9395,
      "y": 13248,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1520,
      "label": "Use WinRM, WinRS or PowerShell remoting",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:move-rdp",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 9395,
      "y": 14893,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1352,
      "label": "Obtain an authorized RDP interactive session",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:move-auth-material",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 9395,
      "y": 16370,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 1731,
      "label": "Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "method-group:S17",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 9395,
      "y": 18226,
      "width": 4080,
      "height": 838,
      "label": "Evaluate a direct Net-NTLMv2 relay path without spoofing",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "topic:lateral-movement",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9420,
      "y": 440,
      "width": 1800,
      "height": 140,
      "text": "# Move to another host\n\nStart with material tied to a known identity and a destination candidate; neither valid authentication nor remote execution rights are assumed.",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:lateral-movement:home",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9420,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 240,
      "text": "## Investigation flow\n\nMove to another host\n\n · \n\nBranches describe evidence and missing conditions. Follow one useful lead, then return to unfinished coverage.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:lateral-movement:check-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9920,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "## Test the destination from the real source\n\nA working password on one service does not establish execution permission on another host.\n\n```bash\nnmap -Pn -sT -p 135,445,3389,5985,5986 TARGET\ngetent hosts TARGET_HOST\n```\n\n**Match route, destination service and effective authorization — on this canvas**"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:lateral-movement:check-0-finding-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10970,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### WinRM is reachable and the account has endpoint rights\n\nUse the WinRM procedure and verify the resulting token.\n\n**Use WinRM, WinRS or PowerShell remoting — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:lateral-movement:check-0-finding-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10970,
      "y": 845,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### SMB/RPC is reachable and service-control rights are confirmed\n\nUse the service-execution procedure with a separate output path.\n\n**Execute through uploaded service creation using PsExec — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:lateral-movement:check-0-fallback",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11740,
      "y": 620,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Unresolved / alternate check\n\nOnly the listener is reachable: inspect actual endpoint authorization before selecting an execution tool.\n\n**Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication — on this canvas**",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:lateral-movement:check-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9920,
      "y": 1250,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 348,
      "text": "## Match password, hash, key or ticket to the client\n\nUse the existing Impacket/NetExec protocol-specific examples; do not treat successful authentication as remote execution.\n\n```bash\nklist\ngetent hosts TARGET_HOST\ndate -u\n```\n\n**Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication — on this canvas**"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:lateral-movement:check-1-finding-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10970,
      "y": 1250,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Accepted authentication plus remote service rights\n\nCheck share/SCM permissions and output reachability.\n\n**Execute through uploaded service creation using PsExec — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:lateral-movement:check-1-finding-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10970,
      "y": 1475,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### WMI/task rights with RPC/DCOM connectivity\n\nCheck the exact namespace/task authorization and output channel.\n\n**Execute through WMI or native CIM over DCOM — on this canvas**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "flow:lateral-movement:check-1-fallback",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11740,
      "y": 1250,
      "width": 610,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Unresolved / alternate check\n\nThe artifact is rejected: recheck identity scope, material format, service name and transport.\n\n[[tracks/05 Credentials.canvas|Classify the artifact and its identity context → 05 Credentials]]",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "notes:lateral-movement",
      "type": "file",
      "file": "notes/lateral-movement.md",
      "x": 9420,
      "y": 1885,
      "width": 2100,
      "height": 850
    },
    {
      "id": "notes-label:lateral-movement",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11710,
      "y": 1885,
      "width": 1400,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "## Full procedures and alternatives\n\nThe adjacent embedded note is readable here. Scroll inside it for complete variants. Commands and decisions continue below.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-preflight:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9430,
      "y": 3160,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Match route, destination service and effective authorization\n\nA credential appears valid but the destination's usable access is unknown",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-preflight:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9930,
      "y": 3120,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nnmap -Pn -sT -p 135,445,3389,5985,5986 TARGET\ngetent hosts TARGET_HOST\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-preflight:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10860,
      "y": 3100,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nSMB/RPC are transport candidates while WinRM is not yet reachable; dynamic RPC and authorization are still untested.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-preflight:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10860,
      "y": 3346,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nProbe the destination from the real source. Check DNS/service names and each required SMB/RPC/WinRM endpoint, then test effective service authorization. An open port and an accepted password do not establish a working remote execution method.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-preflight:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 3050,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nOne compatible service accepts the identity and authorized operation: choose that movement mechanism.\n\n**Verify:** Record exact source, credential type, destination name/service and successfully permitted operation.\n\n[[notes/lateral-movement.md#move-preflight|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-preflight:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 3391,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe intended protocol is conclusively unavailable from this source: reject that route/service combination.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-preflight:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 3612,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nOpen 135 does not settle dynamic RPC; an SMB admin indicator does not settle WMI/WinRM/RDP.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-preflight:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 3050,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nnmap -Pn -sT -sV -p 135,139,445,3389,5985,5986 TARGET -oN movement-preflight.txt\ngetent hosts TARGET_HOST\ndate -u\n```\n\n[[notes/lateral-movement.md#move-preflight|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-preflight:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 3416,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Execute through uploaded service creation using PsExec\n\n**When:** A destination grants administrative-share write and service-control rights\n\n**Still required:** SMB/SCM reachability, writable required share, effective service-creation/start rights and an accepted password/hash or supported Kerberos context\n\n**Execute through uploaded service creation using PsExec — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-preflight:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 3771,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Execute through WMI or native CIM over DCOM\n\n**When:** A destination exposes WMI/DCOM and the identity has useful namespace/process rights\n\n**Still required:** RPC endpoint mapper plus negotiated dynamic ports; effective WMI/DCOM rights; the selected output path may additionally need SMB\n\n**Execute through WMI or native CIM over DCOM — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-preflight:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 4102,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use WinRM, WinRS or PowerShell remoting\n\n**When:** A WinRM listener and a candidate endpoint-authorized account\n\n**Still required:** Reachable HTTP(S) listener, accepted authentication and endpoint/session configuration permissions; hash/ticket support depends on client/context\n\n**Use WinRM, WinRS or PowerShell remoting — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-preflight:next-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 4433,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Obtain an authorized RDP interactive session\n\n**When:** RDP is reachable and the identity may have remote-interactive logon rights\n\n**Still required:** Allowed account/session policy and compatible client/NLA/TLS; hash-based Restricted Admin has additional supported-policy/admin requirements\n\n**Obtain an authorized RDP interactive session — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-preflight:next-4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 4788,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Execute through remote Task Scheduler\n\n**When:** The identity has remote task rights and a compatible output path\n\n**Still required:** Task Scheduler RPC reachability, effective task-creation rights and the required administrative output access\n\n**Execute through remote Task Scheduler — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-preflight:next-5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 5095,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Execute through an authorized DCOM application object\n\n**When:** A usable remote COM application and effective activation/method rights\n\n**Still required:** RPC/dynamic-port route, allowed DCOM activation and application method, supported authentication and target component\n\n**Execute through an authorized DCOM application object — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-services:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9430,
      "y": 5726,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Execute through uploaded service creation using PsExec\n\nA destination grants administrative-share write and service-control rights",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-services:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9930,
      "y": 5686,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nnxc smb TARGET -d DOMAIN -u USER -p 'PASSWORD' --shares\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-services:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10860,
      "y": 5666,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nAdministrative-share control is one PsExec prerequisite, not proof of every service/pipe operation.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-services:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10860,
      "y": 5912,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nValidate actual SCM rights, binary compatibility, service start and named-pipe path; check the final execution identity.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-services:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 5616,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nAll share/SCM/pipe conditions hold and remote effect is observed: use the service-upload method.\n\n**Verify:** Verify destination and represented execution identity, not only service creation or tool success.\n\n[[notes/lateral-movement.md#move-services|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-services:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 5957,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nADMIN$ is unwritable or SCM creation is denied: reject this specific PsExec route.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-services:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 6178,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA tool's admin label alone leaves exact method authorization unresolved.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-services:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 5616,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\n# Password\nimpacket-psexec 'DOMAIN/USER:PASSWORD@TARGET'\n\n# NT hash / Pass-the-Hash\nimpacket-psexec -hashes :NT_HASH 'DOMAIN/USER@TARGET'\n```\n\n[[notes/lateral-movement.md#move-services|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-services:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 6030,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Establish Windows token, host and process context\n\n**When:** A new Windows session or claimed administrator/SYSTEM transition\n\n**Still required:** A functioning command channel and the actual effective token/process context\n\n[[tracks/08 Windows Privilege Escalation.canvas|Establish Windows token, host and process context → 08 Windows Privilege Escalation]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-services:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 6337,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Obtain accessible live logon-session credential material\n\n**When:** A controlled Windows host may hold useful logged-on identities\n\n**Still required:** Required process/host privileges, useful sessions and compatible architecture; PPL/Credential Guard/protection may prevent access or remove material\n\n**Obtain accessible live logon-session credential material — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-services:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 6668,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Execute commands through service command lines and SMB output\n\n**When:** SCM rights and SMB output access exist but an uploaded service binary is unsuitable\n\n**Still required:** Accepted authentication, service create/start rights and the selected output-share/server path\n\n**Execute commands through service command lines and SMB output — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-smbexec:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9430,
      "y": 7299,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Execute commands through service command lines and SMB output\n\nSCM rights and SMB output access exist but an uploaded service binary is unsuitable",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-smbexec:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9930,
      "y": 7259,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nnxc smb TARGET -d DOMAIN -u USER -p 'PASSWORD' --shares\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-smbexec:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10860,
      "y": 7239,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA share and possible service rights suggest the command-line service route, whose output still has its own access path.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-smbexec:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10860,
      "y": 7485,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nConfirm service create/start, exact output mode/share and command effect independently from retrieved stdout.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-smbexec:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 7189,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe service command executes and its selected output is available: choose SMBExec.\n\n**Verify:** Verify command effect separately from successful output retrieval and remove created artifacts as appropriate.\n\n[[notes/lateral-movement.md#move-smbexec|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-smbexec:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 7530,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nSCM creation is denied: reject service-command execution despite SMB login.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-smbexec:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 7727,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nNo stdout may be output-share failure rather than failed process execution.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-smbexec:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 7189,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nimpacket-smbexec 'DOMAIN/USER:PASSWORD@TARGET'\nimpacket-smbexec -hashes :NT_HASH 'DOMAIN/USER@TARGET'\n```\n\n[[notes/lateral-movement.md#move-smbexec|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-smbexec:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 7531,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Establish Windows token, host and process context\n\n**When:** A new Windows session or claimed administrator/SYSTEM transition\n\n**Still required:** A functioning command channel and the actual effective token/process context\n\n[[tracks/08 Windows Privilege Escalation.canvas|Establish Windows token, host and process context → 08 Windows Privilege Escalation]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-smbexec:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 7838,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Execute through uploaded service creation using PsExec\n\n**When:** A destination grants administrative-share write and service-control rights\n\n**Still required:** SMB/SCM reachability, writable required share, effective service-creation/start rights and an accepted password/hash or supported Kerberos context\n\n**Execute through uploaded service creation using PsExec — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-smbexec:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 8193,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Diagnose connection direction, listener and session failures in order\n\n**When:** Command execution or payload delivery exists but the expected usable channel does not\n\n**Still required:** A recorded first execution proof, correct advertised route, active compatible listener and observable connection evidence\n\n[[tracks/11 Execution Troubleshooting.canvas|Diagnose connection direction, listener and session failures in order → 11 Execution Troubleshooting]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-tasks:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9430,
      "y": 8824,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Execute through remote Task Scheduler\n\nThe identity has remote task rights and a compatible output path",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-tasks:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9930,
      "y": 8784,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nTest-NetConnection TARGET -Port 135\nTest-NetConnection TARGET -Port 445\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-tasks:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10860,
      "y": 8764,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe required network services are candidates; a task cannot be assumed creatable from port results.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-tasks:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10860,
      "y": 9010,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCheck negotiated RPC reachability, task-create permission, actual principal and administrative output channel.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-tasks:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 8714,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nTask creation/execution and the bounded effect are verified: choose ATExec.\n\n**Verify:** Verify the actual task effect/principal and destination, not task registration alone.\n\n[[notes/lateral-movement.md#move-tasks|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-tasks:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 9031,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe account lacks remote task rights: reject this method while retaining other service access.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-tasks:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 9252,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA task-run request accepted without process/effect evidence is inconclusive.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-tasks:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 8714,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nimpacket-atexec 'DOMAIN/USER:PASSWORD@TARGET_HOST' \"cmd.exe /c hostname & whoami\"\nimpacket-atexec -hashes :NT_HASH 'DOMAIN/USER@TARGET_HOST' \"cmd.exe /c hostname & whoami\"\n```\n\n[[notes/lateral-movement.md#move-tasks|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-tasks:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 9056,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Verify command execution, host and represented identity\n\n**When:** A PoC, injected command or remote client reports execution\n\n**Still required:** A functioning execution primitive and an observable output or controlled side effect\n\n[[tracks/06 Shells and Transfers.canvas|Verify command execution, host and represented identity → 06 Shells and Transfers]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-tasks:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 9363,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Establish Windows token, host and process context\n\n**When:** A new Windows session or claimed administrator/SYSTEM transition\n\n**Still required:** A functioning command channel and the actual effective token/process context\n\n[[tracks/08 Windows Privilege Escalation.canvas|Establish Windows token, host and process context → 08 Windows Privilege Escalation]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-tasks:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 9670,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Match route, destination service and effective authorization\n\n**When:** A credential appears valid but the destination's usable access is unknown\n\n**Still required:** Real source-to-service route, correct identity context and protocol-specific execution/logon rights\n\n**Match route, destination service and effective authorization — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-wmi:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9430,
      "y": 10301,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Execute through WMI or native CIM over DCOM\n\nA destination exposes WMI/DCOM and the identity has useful namespace/process rights",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-wmi:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9930,
      "y": 10261,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nTest-NetConnection TARGET -Port 135\nTest-NetConnection TARGET -Port 445\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-wmi:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10860,
      "y": 10241,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nPort 135 and an output route justify further checks but do not prove a WMI process can be created.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-wmi:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10860,
      "y": 10487,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nValidate dynamic ports, DCOM/WMI authorization, native CIM transport choice and actual effect.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-wmi:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 10191,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nAuthorized process creation plus a working observation/output path exists: use WMI/CIM.\n\n**Verify:** Verify destination process/effect and execution identity separately from captured stdout.\n\n[[notes/lateral-movement.md#move-wmi|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-wmi:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 10532,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe required namespace/activation permission is denied: reject that identity's WMI route.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-wmi:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 10753,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nExecution may succeed with failed output retrieval; inspect a controlled effect before concluding.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-wmi:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 10191,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\nimpacket-wmiexec 'DOMAIN/USER:PASSWORD@TARGET'\nimpacket-wmiexec -hashes :NT_HASH 'DOMAIN/USER@TARGET'\n```\n\n[[notes/lateral-movement.md#move-wmi|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-wmi:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 10533,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Verify command execution, host and represented identity\n\n**When:** A PoC, injected command or remote client reports execution\n\n**Still required:** A functioning execution primitive and an observable output or controlled side effect\n\n[[tracks/06 Shells and Transfers.canvas|Verify command execution, host and represented identity → 06 Shells and Transfers]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-wmi:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 10840,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Diagnose connection direction, listener and session failures in order\n\n**When:** Command execution or payload delivery exists but the expected usable channel does not\n\n**Still required:** A recorded first execution proof, correct advertised route, active compatible listener and observable connection evidence\n\n[[tracks/11 Execution Troubleshooting.canvas|Diagnose connection direction, listener and session failures in order → 11 Execution Troubleshooting]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-wmi:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 11171,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use WinRM, WinRS or PowerShell remoting\n\n**When:** A WinRM listener and a candidate endpoint-authorized account\n\n**Still required:** Reachable HTTP(S) listener, accepted authentication and endpoint/session configuration permissions; hash/ticket support depends on client/context\n\n**Use WinRM, WinRS or PowerShell remoting — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-dcom:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9430,
      "y": 11802,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Execute through an authorized DCOM application object\n\nA usable remote COM application and effective activation/method rights",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-dcom:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9930,
      "y": 11762,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nTest-NetConnection TARGET -Port 135\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-dcom:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10860,
      "y": 11742,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA named application and route form a candidate; component availability and allowed activation/method remain separate.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-dcom:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10860,
      "y": 11988,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCheck dynamic RPC, actual class/rights, authentication/tool support, method and verifiable output/effect.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-dcom:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 11692,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe intended authorized application method produces the remote effect: choose this DCOM route.\n\n**Verify:** Verify the actual destination effect and identity; COM object creation alone does not prove command execution.\n\n[[notes/lateral-movement.md#move-dcom|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-dcom:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 12033,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe component is absent or activation is denied: reject that class-based chain.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-dcom:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 12254,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA created COM object without command/effect evidence leaves execution unproved.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-dcom:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 11692,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 396,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```powershell\n$Type = [type]::GetTypeFromProgID('MMC20.Application.1','TARGET_HOST')\n$Object = [Activator]::CreateInstance($Type)\n$Object.Document.ActiveView.ExecuteShellCommand(\n  'cmd.exe',\n  $null,\n  '/c hostname > C:\\Windows\\Temp\\movement-proof.txt',\n  '7'\n)\n```\n\n[[notes/lateral-movement.md#move-dcom|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-dcom:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 12178,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Verify command execution, host and represented identity\n\n**When:** A PoC, injected command or remote client reports execution\n\n**Still required:** A functioning execution primitive and an observable output or controlled side effect\n\n[[tracks/06 Shells and Transfers.canvas|Verify command execution, host and represented identity → 06 Shells and Transfers]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-dcom:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 12485,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Match route, destination service and effective authorization\n\n**When:** A credential appears valid but the destination's usable access is unknown\n\n**Still required:** Real source-to-service route, correct identity context and protocol-specific execution/logon rights\n\n**Match route, destination service and effective authorization — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-dcom:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 12816,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Repair quoting, encoding and command-length boundaries\n\n**When:** A simple command works while a longer or nested payload fails\n\n**Still required:** Known outer request/template/database parser and inner shell; correct character encoding and transport length\n\n[[tracks/11 Execution Troubleshooting.canvas|Repair quoting, encoding and command-length boundaries → 11 Execution Troubleshooting]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-winrm:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9430,
      "y": 13423,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Use WinRM, WinRS or PowerShell remoting\n\nA WinRM listener and a candidate endpoint-authorized account",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-winrm:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9930,
      "y": 13383,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 204,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nTest-NetConnection TARGET -Port 5985\nTest-NetConnection TARGET -Port 5986\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-winrm:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10860,
      "y": 13363,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nA reachable endpoint plus a known credential is a candidate, not proof the account may enter that remoting session.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-winrm:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10860,
      "y": 13609,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nVerify accepted authentication, correct name/TLS context, endpoint rights and any second-hop requirements.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-winrm:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 13313,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe endpoint opens the intended session and identity is verified: choose WinRM/WinRS/remoting.\n\n**Verify:** Verify hostname, whoami /all and the actual session configuration/rights.\n\n[[notes/lateral-movement.md#move-winrm|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-winrm:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 13654,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nA valid account is denied the endpoint: reject that session configuration for this identity.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-winrm:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 13875,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nSecond-hop resource failure does not disprove the first WinRM authentication.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-winrm:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 13313,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 396,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\n# Password; omit -p to prompt where supported\nevil-winrm -i TARGET_HOST -u USER -p 'PASSWORD'\n\n# NT hash\nevil-winrm -i TARGET_HOST -u USER -H NT_HASH\n\n# HTTPS listener\nevil-winrm -i TARGET_HOST -u USER -p 'PASSWORD' -S -P 5986\n```\n\n[[notes/lateral-movement.md#move-winrm|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-winrm:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 13799,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Establish Windows token, host and process context\n\n**When:** A new Windows session or claimed administrator/SYSTEM transition\n\n**Still required:** A functioning command channel and the actual effective token/process context\n\n[[tracks/08 Windows Privilege Escalation.canvas|Establish Windows token, host and process context → 08 Windows Privilege Escalation]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-winrm:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 14106,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Obtain accessible live logon-session credential material\n\n**When:** A controlled Windows host may hold useful logged-on identities\n\n**Still required:** Required process/host privileges, useful sessions and compatible architecture; PPL/Credential Guard/protection may prevent access or remove material\n\n**Obtain accessible live logon-session credential material — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-winrm:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 14437,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Match route, destination service and effective authorization\n\n**When:** A credential appears valid but the destination's usable access is unknown\n\n**Still required:** Real source-to-service route, correct identity context and protocol-specific execution/logon rights\n\n**Match route, destination service and effective authorization — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-rdp:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9430,
      "y": 15068,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Obtain an authorized RDP interactive session\n\nRDP is reachable and the identity may have remote-interactive logon rights",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-rdp:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9930,
      "y": 15028,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nTest-NetConnection TARGET -Port 3389\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-rdp:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10860,
      "y": 15008,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nRDP transport does not grant desktop access; Restricted Admin/hash use has additional requirements.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-rdp:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10860,
      "y": 15254,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nCheck NLA/TLS, identity qualification, logon authorization and the chosen authentication mode.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-rdp:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 14958,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe authorized interactive logon opens under the verified token: choose RDP.\n\n**Verify:** Verify destination, user/token and permitted desktop actions; keep credentials out of reusable screenshots/notes.\n\n[[notes/lateral-movement.md#move-rdp|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-rdp:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 15275,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nThe account lacks the required logon right or the hash route lacks Restricted Admin support: reject that variant.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-rdp:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 15496,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nA generic connection error requires separating client/protocol/policy before judging the credential.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-rdp:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 14958,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```bash\ncommand -v xfreerdp3 || command -v xfreerdp\n```\n\n[[notes/lateral-movement.md#move-rdp|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-rdp:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 15276,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 252,
      "text": "### Establish Windows token, host and process context\n\n**When:** A new Windows session or claimed administrator/SYSTEM transition\n\n**Still required:** A functioning command channel and the actual effective token/process context\n\n[[tracks/08 Windows Privilege Escalation.canvas|Establish Windows token, host and process context → 08 Windows Privilege Escalation]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-rdp:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 15583,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Recover Windows application, history and stored-credential artifacts\n\n**When:** Readable application configuration, unattended setup, PowerShell trails or Credential Manager entries\n\n**Still required:** Artifact read permission and exact protecting identity/context for saved or DPAPI material\n\n[[tracks/08 Windows Privilege Escalation.canvas|Recover Windows application, history and stored-credential artifacts → 08 Windows Privilege Escalation]]",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-rdp:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 15914,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication\n\n**When:** A password, actual NT hash, AES/NT long-term key or ticket is available\n\n**Still required:** Credential type accepted by the chosen protocol/client, correct identity/domain, naming/time and destination authorization\n\n**Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-auth-material:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9430,
      "y": 16545,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Select password, NT hash, key-to-ticket or ticket authentication\n\nA password, actual NT hash, AES/NT long-term key or ticket is available",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-auth-material:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9930,
      "y": 16505,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nklist\ngetent hosts TARGET_HOST\ndate -u\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-auth-material:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10860,
      "y": 16485,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nThe cache permits investigating a matching CIFS action, not arbitrary WinRM or a new TGS without a TGT/KDC route.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-auth-material:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10860,
      "y": 16731,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nMatch NTLM versus Kerberos support, account/domain, key/encryption policy, name/time and destination rights.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-auth-material:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 16435,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nThe selected client/service accepts the exact material and action: use that method.\n\n**Verify:** Verify exact material type, represented network identity and successful destination action.\n\n[[notes/lateral-movement.md#move-auth-material|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-auth-material:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 16776,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 156,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nOnly a challenge response is available for a direct NT-hash client: reject the type mismatch.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-auth-material:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 16997,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nAn unlabelled hash or unknown ticket lifetime requires classification first.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-auth-material:action",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 16435,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Procedure entry — full sequence in the note\n\n```text\nNT HASH -> NTLM CHALLENGE/RESPONSE -> TARGET SERVICE\n```\n\n[[notes/lateral-movement.md#move-auth-material|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-auth-material:next-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 16753,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 300,
      "text": "### Execute through uploaded service creation using PsExec\n\n**When:** A destination grants administrative-share write and service-control rights\n\n**Still required:** SMB/SCM reachability, writable required share, effective service-creation/start rights and an accepted password/hash or supported Kerberos context\n\n**Execute through uploaded service creation using PsExec — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-auth-material:next-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 17108,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Execute through WMI or native CIM over DCOM\n\n**When:** A destination exposes WMI/DCOM and the identity has useful namespace/process rights\n\n**Still required:** RPC endpoint mapper plus negotiated dynamic ports; effective WMI/DCOM rights; the selected output path may additionally need SMB\n\n**Execute through WMI or native CIM over DCOM — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-auth-material:next-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 17439,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Use WinRM, WinRS or PowerShell remoting\n\n**When:** A WinRM listener and a candidate endpoint-authorized account\n\n**Still required:** Reachable HTTP(S) listener, accepted authentication and endpoint/session configuration permissions; hash/ticket support depends on client/context\n\n**Use WinRM, WinRS or PowerShell remoting — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:move-auth-material:next-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12490,
      "y": 17770,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 276,
      "text": "### Inventory, convert and import tickets in the correct logon context\n\n**When:** A valid ticket/cache or a long-term key that can request a TGT\n\n**Still required:** Matching client/realm/service, valid lifetime, compatible format and available KDC/service routes; ticket import affects a specific context\n\n**Inventory, convert and import tickets in the correct logon context — on this canvas**",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S17:start",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9430,
      "y": 18401,
      "width": 350,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "## Evaluate a direct Net-NTLMv2 relay path without spoofing\n\nan explicitly authorized, live NTLM authentication source is already present and a different receiver target is relevant. A saved Net-NTLMv2 response alone does not enter this state.",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S17:discover",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9930,
      "y": 18361,
      "width": 780,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### Discover\n\n```text\nSee the linked discovery procedure.\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S17:interpret",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10860,
      "y": 18341,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 180,
      "text": "### What the output establishes\n\nidentify source protocol/event, relayed principal, receiver protocol/host and source-to-target reachability. For a selected SMB receiver, inspect signing with nmap -p 445 --script smb2-security-mode TARGET.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S17:validate",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10860,
      "y": 18611,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 228,
      "text": "### Missing prerequisite\n\nreceiver accepts NTLM, signing/EPA/channel binding/reflection protections permit the exchange, and the relayed principal has one useful target operation. Current exam rules prohibit poisoning/spoofing; Responder name-resolution poisoning is never the source in the exam workflow.\nACTION PROCEDURE PENDING: discovery/validation only.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S17:enabled",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 18291,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 324,
      "text": "### Condition confirmed\n\nsource + compatible receiver + useful authorization established → ready for RW09 procedure; signing/protocol/authorization decisively blocks it → ruled out for that receiver; protection or source-event behavior unresolved → inconclusive.\n\n**Verify:** define success as the chosen receiver operation under the relayed identity, not merely an inbound connection or captured challenge-response.\n\n[[notes/lateral-movement.md#S17|Full note & variants]]",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S17:ruledout",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 18680,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Condition disproved here\n\nFollow the denied/absent-condition outcome in the linked procedure.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "method:S17:unknown",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11640,
      "y": 18877,
      "width": 620,
      "height": 132,
      "text": "### Evidence inconclusive\n\nResolve the missing condition; do not infer execution from visibility.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "track-title",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 2300,
      "height": 270,
      "color": "5",
      "text": "# 09 Active Directory\n\nAll workflows, commands, result interpretations and method connections for this track are on this canvas. Embedded notes contain the complete procedures and variants.\n\n[[START.canvas|Choose another track]]\n\nCross-track results link directly to the receiving track."
    }
  ],
